WEBVTT

1
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.403
<i>This is Zero One Alpha.
We have secured Falcon.</i>

2
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.604
<i>I say again, we have secured Falcon.</i>

3
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.246
By the time I count to ten...

4
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.527
...you will have told me
exactly what I need to know.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.000
If not...

6
00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.047
...the number ten will be the
last thing you will ever hear.

7
00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.240
One

8
00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.043
Two

9
00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.360
Three

10
00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.480
Four

11
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.720
Five

12
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.760
Six

13
00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:03.880
Seven

14
00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:04.563
Eight

15
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.364
<i>Grenade! Sir, get back!</i>

16
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.051
Shit.

17
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.290
Fucking missed it.

18
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.882
How did I fucking miss it?

19
00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.684
Merlin, I apologize for putting
you in this position.

20
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.405
You trained him well.

21
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.970
James...

22
00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.202
training is over.

23
00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.442
Welcome to Kingsman.

24
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.246
Lancelot.

25
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.401
Sir.

26
00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.770
I'll deal with this mess personally.

27
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.923
<i>I very much regret that your husband's
bravery can't be publicly celebrated.</i>

28
00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.406
I hope you understand.

29
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.085
How can I understand?

30
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.242
You won't tell me anything.

31
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.600
I didn't even know
he wasn't with his squad.

32
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.000
I'm so sorry, I can't say more.

33
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.449
But I would like to present you
with this Medal of Valor...

34
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.969
and if you look closely on the back,
there's a number.

35
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.846
And as a more concrete gesture
of our gratitude...

36
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.923
we'd like to offer you...

37
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.441
Let's call it a favor.

38
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.130
The nature of it is your choice.

39
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.645
Just tell the operator...

40
00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.522
"oxfords not brogues,"
and then I'll know it's you.

41
00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.531
I don't want your help!

42
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.081
I want my husband back!

43
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.126
What's your name, young man?

44
00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.680
Eggsy.

45
00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.125
Hello, Eggsy.

46
00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.531
Can I see that?

47
00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.288
You take care of this, Eggsy.

48
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.691
All right?

49
00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.205
And take care of your mum, too.

50
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.726
So sorry, Professor Arnold.
Just a tiny bit more.

51
00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.406
For God's sakes, just rip it off.

52
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:04.087
I'm under very strict instructions
not to hurt you.

53
00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.521
Look, you've made a mistake.

54
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.445
I'm a university lecturer.
I've got no money.

55
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.090
This isn't about money.

56
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.208
Our boss just wants to talk to you.

57
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.283
Am I meant to find that reassuring?

58
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.568
He'll be here soon. He'll explain.

59
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.370
Do you like whiskey?

60
00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.771
Red, get the '62 Dalmore.

61
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.129
Honestly, this whiskey, it's amazing.

62
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.249
You will shit.

63
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.923
I suppose asking to borrow
a cup of sugar is a step too far?

64
00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.811
Professor Arnold,
I'm here to take you home.

65
00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.443
1962 Dalmore.

66
00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.683
It'd be a sin to spill any.

67
00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.805
Don't you think?

68
00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.688
Can you hold these? Please?

69
00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:34.960
Thank you.

70
00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.568
Everything is clean.

71
00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.045
My kind of welcome.

72
00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.568
No stomach for violence.

73
00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.643
I mean, literally,
I see one drop of blood...

74
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.723
that is me done.

75
00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.081
I'm like...

76
00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.571
projectile.

77
00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.927
Listen, I'm so sorry...

78
00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:16.450
you had to witness all this unpleasantness
due to our uninvited guest.

79
00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.770
But I promise you, by the time
I've found out who he works for...

80
00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:25.244
you and I will be the best of friends.

81
00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.888
To the shop, please.

82
00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.520
Arthur's in the dining room, sir.

83
00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.006
Arthur.

84
00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.406
Galahad.

85
00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:16.282
The others were beginning to wonder
if we were going to have a double toast.

86
00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.931
Gentlemen, I'm thankful to
say it's been 17 years...

87
00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.487
since we last had occasion
to use this decanter.

88
00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.763
Lancelot was an outstanding agent,
and a true Kingsman.

89
00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.371
He will be sorely missed.

90
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.921
To Lancelot.

91
00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.410
To Lancelot.

92
00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.480
I intend to start the selection process
for Lancelot's replacement tomorrow.

93
00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:49.161
I want each of you
to propose a candidate...

94
00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.687
and have them report to UK HQ...

95
00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.008
no later than 9 p.m. GMT.

96
00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:55.640
Thank you.

97
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Merlin.

98
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.530
Come in.

99
00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.566
Lancelot was investigating
a group of mercenaries...

100
00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.451
who were experimenting
with biological weaponry.

101
00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:08.680
Glasses, gentlemen, please.

102
00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.601
Uganda, 2012.

103
00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.290
Synthetic cathinones.

104
00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.887
They put it in the water supply
of a guerrilla army base.

105
00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.283
Rage, cannibalism, multiple fatalities.

106
00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.130
Chechnya, 2013.

107
00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.090
Insurgents turned on one another.

108
00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:31.006
Indisputably, the work of our mercenaries,
but no trace of any chemicals of any kind.

109
00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.320
So what happened to Lancelot?

110
00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.289
He tracked them to this property
in Argentina.

111
00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.766
While he had them under surveillance...

112
00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.763
he became aware
they'd effected a kidnapping.

113
00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:44.605
So he executed a solo rescue mission,
which failed.

114
00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.005
This is his last transmission.

115
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.526
- Who is he?
- Some climate change doomsayer.

116
00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.320
Expounds something
called "Gaia theory"...

117
00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.124
about the world healing itself,
or some such.

118
00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.171
But what's curious,
is he's not actually missing.

119
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.967
This is Professor Arnold...

120
00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.168
at Imperial College this morning.

121
00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.004
It's all yours.

122
00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.487
And don't forget
your membership proposal.

123
00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.723
Try picking a more suitable
candidate this time.

124
00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.769
17 years and still...

125
00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.561
evolving with the times remains
an entirely foreign concept to you.

126
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.809
Need I remind you, I wouldn't be here
if it weren't for that young man?

127
00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.566
He was as much Kingsman
material as any of them.

128
00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:25.926
More so.

129
00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.124
But he wasn't exactly one of us, was he?

130
00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:33.487
Let's face it, Galahad,
your little experiment failed.

131
00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.686
With respect, Arthur, you're a snob.

132
00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:38.961
"With respect"?

133
00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.322
The world is changing.

134
00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:46.485
There's a reason why aristocrats
developed weak chins.

135
00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.240
Eggsy?

136
00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.204
Eggsy, come here.

137
00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.209
- Got any Rizla, babe?
- No.

138
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.408
Why don't you do your mum a favor,
go down to the shop and get some?

139
00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:18.891
- Get them yourself.
- Oi.

140
00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.691
What have I said to you
about speaking to Dean like that?

141
00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.327
Three's a crowd, innit?
Why don't Dean's poodle go?

142
00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.970
I'll tell you what.

143
00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:28.884
Why don't you take this,
go and get some Rizlas...

144
00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.000
get yourself some sweets?
And while you're gone...

145
00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.964
we'll show your mother
how three can be good company.

146
00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.560
Thanks, babe.

147
00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.964
There we go.

148
00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.166
Is that better?

149
00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.321
If Dean treats your mum so bad,
why doesn't she leave him?

150
00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.448
Low self-esteem. That's her problem.

151
00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.400
Fuck off.
Why would she have low self-esteem?

152
00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.369
Eggsy's mum is well fit.

153
00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.882
- No offense, bruv.
- It's all right.

154
00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.121
One of these days,
I'm gonna smash his face in.

155
00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.725
Are you mental, cuz?

156
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.600
He'd just get that lot to do you,
and then pretend he knew nothing...

157
00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.040
...about it.

158
00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.767
You think you can chat shit about us
and we won't do nothing...

159
00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:32.082
just because our guvnor's
banging Eggsy's mum?

160
00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.083
Pretty much, yeah.

161
00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.402
Bruv, just leave it.
Let's just go, man.

162
00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.560
It's not worth it.

163
00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.246
You boys have outstayed your welcome.

164
00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:41.560
Leave.

165
00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.321
What?

166
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.923
I'm sorry about that, bruv.

167
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.000
Yeah.

168
00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.127
Mug.

169
00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.402
They weren't fucking worth it, boys.

170
00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.768
It's freezing.
Why are we walking?

171
00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.763
You jacked his fucking car keys, bruv?

172
00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.446
Yeah. Now, we're gonna nick his car.

173
00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.451
Shit!

174
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.810
Hold on, boys.

175
00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.049
Hey, that's my fucking car!

176
00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.441
Hey! Hey! Eggsy!

177
00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.648
I swear, you want to fucking stop it!

178
00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.366
You're a fucking dead man! Stop it!

179
00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.320
I'm gonna fucking have ya!

180
00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.965
Floor it, Eggsy!

181
00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.120
Floor it!

182
00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.080
Wanker!

183
00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.445
Yeah, Dean. Look, it's me.

184
00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.602
Eggsy just stole my fucking car.

185
00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.604
I've come out the pub,
he's done 15 donuts in my fucking face...

186
00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.330
and he's drove off.

187
00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.608
No, I can't have it!
He's disrespecting me.

188
00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.967
And that means,
he's disrespecting you.

189
00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.004
Hold up! What the...?

190
00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:39.840
Dickhead.

191
00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.643
Foxes are vermin, cuz.

192
00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.245
Should've driven it over.

193
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:47.368
Should've done a lot of things.

194
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.204
I'll sort this. Get out of the car.

195
00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.888
I said, get out of the fucking car!

196
00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.848
<i>Eggsy, there is no such thing
as honor amongst thieves.</i>

197
00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.561
Now, you can start giving me some names
of the boys you were with...

198
00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.565
or you go down.

199
00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.771
It's up to you.

200
00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:15.680
I want to exercise
my right to a phone call.

201
00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.762
Well, I hope it's to your mum...

202
00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.447
to tell her you're gonna be
18 months late for your dinner.

203
00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.767
<i>Customer Complaints, how may I help you?</i>

204
00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.130
My name's Eggsy Unwin.

205
00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.763
Sorry, Gary Unwin.
And I'm up shit creek.

206
00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:07.240
I'm in Holborn police station...

207
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:09.044
and my mum said to call this number
if ever I needed help.

208
00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.680
<i>I'm sorry, sir. Wrong number.</i>

209
00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:13.211
Wait! Wait!

210
00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.201
Oxfords not brogues.

211
00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:20.440
<i>Your complaint has been duly noted...</i>

212
00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:23.643
<i>and we hope that we have
not lost you as a loyal customer.</i>

213
00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.041
Yeah.

214
00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.971
You what?

215
00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:41.367
I...

216
00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:42.801
Yeah.

217
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.171
Yes, I totally understand.

218
00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.766
Eggsy.

219
00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:08.886
Would you like a lift home?

220
00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:10.841
Who are you?

221
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.365
The man who got you released.

222
00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.851
That ain't an answer.

223
00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.367
A little gratitude would be nice.

224
00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:20.842
My name is Harry Hart,
and I gave you that medal.

225
00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.402
Your father saved my life.

226
00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:29.808
So before you was a tailor,
was you in the army?

227
00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:31.691
Like an officer.

228
00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.370
Not quite.

229
00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.329
So where was you posted,
Iraq or something?

230
00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.767
Sorry, Eggsy. Classified.

231
00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.365
But my dad saved your life, yeah?

232
00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:44.927
The day your father died,
I missed something.

233
00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.166
And if it weren't for his courage...

234
00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:50.244
my mistake would have cost the lives
of every man present.

235
00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.685
So I owe him.

236
00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:55.888
Your father was a brave man.

237
00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.889
A good man.

238
00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.200
And having read your files...

239
00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.681
I think he'd be bitterly disappointed
in the choices you've made.

240
00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.080
You can't talk to me like that.

241
00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.200
Huge I.Q.

242
00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.129
Great performance at primary school.

243
00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.371
And it all went tits up.

244
00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:12.251
Drugs, petty crime.
Never had a job.

245
00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.084
You think there's a lot of jobs
going around here, do you?

246
00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.730
Doesn't explain
why you gave up your hobbies.

247
00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.491
First prize,
regional Under-10s gymnastics...

248
00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:19.880
two years in a row.

249
00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.247
Your coach had you pegged
as Olympic team material.

250
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.084
Yeah, well, when you grow up around
someone like my stepdad...

251
00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.730
you pick up new hobbies pretty quick.

252
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.609
Of course. Always someone else's fault.

253
00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.040
Who's to blame
for you quitting the Marines?

254
00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.561
You were halfway through training,
doing brilliantly, but you gave up.

255
00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.722
Because my mum went mental.

256
00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.690
Banging on about losing me
as well as my dad.

257
00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:41.286
Didn't want me being cannon fodder
for snobs like you.

258
00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.841
Judging people like me
from your ivory towers...

259
00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.241
with no thought about
why we do what we do.

260
00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.286
We ain't got much choice. You get me?

261
00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.121
And if we was born with the same
silver spoon up our arses...

262
00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:55.124
we'd do just as well as you.
If not, better.

263
00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:58.124
What the fuck you doing here?
You taking the piss?

264
00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.081
Some more examples of young men...

265
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.969
