308
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.930
<i>No ransom has been demanded.</i>

309
00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:09.048
Eggsy, just go, please,
because he's gonna...

310
00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:11.730
No, please, don't hurt him!

311
00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:13.564
Fuck off! Get the fuck away with ya!

312
00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:14.966
Shut the fuck up!

313
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:17.248
Who was with you in that fucking pub?

314
00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.562
I want to know the name of the geezer
you was with.

315
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:21.563
- I wasn't with no one!
- Who was it?

316
00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:23.131
- I don't know what you're on about.
- Who was it?

317
00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:24.441
I don't know
who you're fucking on about!

318
00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:25.726
Fucking tell me his name!

319
00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:28.201
I don't know
who you're fucking on about!

320
00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:33.441
<i>You listen to me!</i>

321
00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:35.568
<i>I want to know who you was with in that pub.
Do you understand?</i>

322
00:24:35.720 --> 00:24:37.609
<i>I want to know his fucking name!</i>

323
00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:40.730
<i>Because, I swear,
I'll rip your head off.</i>

324
00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:43.963
<i>- Tell me!
- I don't know what you're fucking on about!</i>

325
00:24:44.120 --> 00:24:45.167
Just tell him, Eggsy!

326
00:24:45.320 --> 00:24:47.129
Fuck off! Fuck off, Michelle!

327
00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.566
I could kill you right now...

328
00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:51.246
and no one in the whole world
will notice!

329
00:24:51.400 --> 00:24:53.084
<i>But I would.</i>

330
00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:55.083
I have enough evidence
on your activities...

331
00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:57.242
to have you locked up
for the rest of your life...

332
00:24:57.400 --> 00:24:59.641
- Mr. Dean Anthony Baker.
- What the fuck?

333
00:24:59.840 --> 00:25:01.410
<i>So I suggest you leave the boy alone...</i>

334
00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:05.161
<i>or I shall be forced to deliver it
to the appropriate authorities.</i>

335
00:25:06.160 --> 00:25:08.731
<i>Eggsy, meet me at the tailor
I told you about.</i>

336
00:25:08.880 --> 00:25:11.360
What the fuck's going on here?

337
00:25:13.320 --> 00:25:14.526
Eggsy, you fucking maggot!

338
00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:15.886
Hey, we got a racer!

339
00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:17.530
Come here. Hey!

340
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:19.366
Eggsy, you fucking...

341
00:25:19.520 --> 00:25:20.806
Come here, son!

342
00:25:33.240 --> 00:25:34.321
You wanker!

343
00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:36.130
I'll have you, son!

344
00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:03.562
I've never met a tailor before.

345
00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:05.731
But I know you ain't one.

346
00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:11.364
Come with me.

347
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:21.326
Come on in.

348
00:26:27.040 --> 00:26:28.041
What do you see?

349
00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:31.563
Someone who wants to know
what the fuck is going on.

350
00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:35.607
I see a young man with potential.

351
00:26:36.920 --> 00:26:38.684
A young man who is loyal.

352
00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:41.569
Who can do as he's asked.

353
00:26:41.720 --> 00:26:44.530
And who wants to do
something good with his life.

354
00:26:46.120 --> 00:26:48.122
Did you see the film <i>Trading Places?</i>

355
00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:50.205
No.

356
00:26:50.600 --> 00:26:52.125
<i>How about Nikita?</i>

357
00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:54.531
<i>Pretty Woman?</i>

358
00:26:55.440 --> 00:26:56.521
All right.

359
00:26:56.680 --> 00:26:59.729
My point is, that the lack of a silver
spoon has set you on a certain path...

360
00:26:59.880 --> 00:27:01.723
but you needn't stay on it.

361
00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:06.807
If you're prepared to adapt and learn,
you can transform.

362
00:27:07.360 --> 00:27:09.203
Like in <i>My Fair Lady.</i>

363
00:27:10.240 --> 00:27:12.288
Well, you're full of surprises.

364
00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:15.245
Yes, like <i>My Fair Lady.</i>

365
00:27:16.320 --> 00:27:19.608
Only, in this case, I'm offering you
the opportunity to become a Kingsman.

366
00:27:20.280 --> 00:27:21.611
A tailor?

367
00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:23.411
A Kingsman agent.

368
00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:26.246
Like a spy?

369
00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:27.566
Of sorts.

370
00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:30.560
Interested?

371
00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:33.242
You think I've got anything to lose?

372
00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:41.765
Since 1849...

373
00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:46.084
Kingsman tailors have clothed
the world's most powerful individuals.

374
00:27:46.240 --> 00:27:50.928
By 1919, a great number of them
had lost their heirs to World War One.

375
00:27:51.760 --> 00:27:55.082
That meant a lot of money
going uninherited.

376
00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:59.290
And a lot of powerful men with a desire
to preserve peace and protect life.

377
00:27:59.440 --> 00:28:02.364
Our founders realized that they could
channel that wealth and influence...

378
00:28:02.520 --> 00:28:04.170
for the greater good.

379
00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:07.608
And so began our other venture.

380
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:10.761
An independent,
international intelligence agency...

381
00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:14.288
operating at the highest level
of discretion.

382
00:28:15.080 --> 00:28:16.570
Above the politics and bureaucracy...

383
00:28:16.720 --> 00:28:20.930
that undermine the integrity
of government-run spy organizations.

384
00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:24.007
The suit is a modern gentleman's armor.

385
00:28:24.840 --> 00:28:27.923
And the Kingsman agents
are the new knights.

386
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:30.604
How deep does this fucking thing go?

387
00:28:30.760 --> 00:28:31.807
Deep enough.

388
00:29:16.480 --> 00:29:18.164
Shit, we're late.

389
00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:45.366
Your father had the
same look on his face.

390
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:48.405
As did I.

391
00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:51.206
Come on.

392
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.047
Galahad.

393
00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:56.201
My code name.

394
00:29:56.360 --> 00:29:57.850
Late again, sir.

395
00:29:58.200 --> 00:29:59.531
Good luck.

396
00:29:59.880 --> 00:30:01.211
In you go.

397
00:30:12.720 --> 00:30:13.881
Fall in.

398
00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:18.964
Ladies and gentlemen, my name is Merlin.

399
00:30:19.120 --> 00:30:20.201
You are about to embark...

400
00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:23.091
on what is probably the most
dangerous job interview in the world.

401
00:30:23.920 --> 00:30:28.767
One of you, and only one of you,
will become the next Lancelot.

402
00:30:29.520 --> 00:30:32.763
Can anybody tell me what this is?

403
00:30:33.640 --> 00:30:35.244
- Yes?
- Body bag, sir.

404
00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:37.721
Correct. Charlie, isn't it?

405
00:30:37.920 --> 00:30:38.920
Yes, sir.

406
00:30:38.960 --> 00:30:39.722
Good.

407
00:30:39.880 --> 00:30:42.247
In a moment,
you will each collect a body bag.

408
00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:44.249
You will write your name on that bag.

409
00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.843
You will write the details
of your next of kin on that bag.

410
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:51.288
This represents your acknowledgment
of the risks that you are about to face...

411
00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:54.729
as well as your agreement
to strict confidentiality.

412
00:30:54.880 --> 00:30:57.963
Which, incidentally, if you break,
will result in you...

413
00:30:58.240 --> 00:31:00.561
and your next of kin...

414
00:31:01.040 --> 00:31:02.610
being in that bag.

415
00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:05.691
Is that understood?

416
00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:08.361
Excellent.

417
00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:10.246
Fall out.

418
00:31:17.560 --> 00:31:19.961
Roxanne. But call me Roxy.

419
00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:22.131
- I'm Eggsy.
- "Eggy"?

420
00:31:22.280 --> 00:31:23.280
No, "Eggsy".

421
00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:24.771
Eggy?

422
00:31:24.920 --> 00:31:26.046
Where did they dig you up?

423
00:31:26.200 --> 00:31:28.328
You know we're not allowed
to discuss who proposed us.

424
00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:29.766
No need to bite his head off.

425
00:31:29.920 --> 00:31:32.287
Charlie's only making conversation,
right, Charlie?

426
00:31:32.880 --> 00:31:34.120
I'm Digby.

427
00:31:35.400 --> 00:31:36.083
Digby.

428
00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:37.651
Eggy, this is Rufus.

429
00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:39.325
Rufus, Eggy.

430
00:31:41.480 --> 00:31:44.290
So, Eggy, are you Oxford or Cambridge?

431
00:31:44.760 --> 00:31:45.443
Neither.

432
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:46.931
- Saint Andrews?
- Durham?

433
00:31:47.080 --> 00:31:49.003
No, wait, I think we may have met.

434
00:31:49.160 --> 00:31:52.721
Did you serve me at the McDonald's
in Winchester service station?

435
00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:53.840
No.

436
00:31:54.280 --> 00:31:56.806
It's definitely Saint Andrews.

437
00:31:57.360 --> 00:31:58.566
Just ignore them.

438
00:31:58.720 --> 00:31:59.801
You need a pen?

439
00:31:59.960 --> 00:32:00.722
Cheers.

440
00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:02.291
Amelia, isn't it?

441
00:32:02.480 --> 00:32:03.891
Amelia, Eggsy.

442
00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:05.201
Hi, Eggsy.

443
00:32:05.560 --> 00:32:07.324
Don't take any notice of those guys.

444
00:32:07.480 --> 00:32:09.164
That's what I told him.

445
00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:12.686
It's just scare tactics.

446
00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:14.565
Classic army technique.

447
00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:15.881
No one's gonna die.

448
00:32:20.040 --> 00:32:21.246
Shame.

449
00:32:23.360 --> 00:32:25.567
Great. You don't know,
the CIA don't know.

450
00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:28.246
Nobody knows who this guy is?

451
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:30.001
Fine.

452
00:32:30.160 --> 00:32:31.525
Seriously, it's fine.

453
00:32:31.720 --> 00:32:35.566
Well, it's not really fine,
but it's not why I'm here.

454
00:32:35.760 --> 00:32:39.207
Hell, man, you know me.
Money's not my issue.

455
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:41.089
I could've retired
straight out of MIT...

456
00:32:41.240 --> 00:32:43.720
fucked off to some island,
let the business run itself.

457
00:32:43.880 --> 00:32:46.645
Nobody told me
to try and save the planet.

458
00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:48.450
I wanted to.

459
00:32:48.600 --> 00:32:52.321
Climate change research,
lobbying, years of study, billions of dollars...

460
00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:54.289
and you know why I quit?

461
00:32:54.720 --> 00:32:59.487
Because the last time I checked,
the planet was still fucked.

462
00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:02.326
Hence, my epiphany.

463
00:33:02.480 --> 00:33:05.245
Money won't solve this.

464
00:33:05.600 --> 00:33:08.080
Those idiots
who call themselves politicians...

465
00:33:08.240 --> 00:33:12.290
have buried their heads in the sand
and stood for nothing but re-election.

466
00:33:13.080 --> 00:33:17.404
So I spent the last two years
trying to find a real solution.

467
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:19.923
And I found it.

468
00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:24.129
Now, if you really want to make
the world a better place...

469
00:33:24.280 --> 00:33:28.763
I suggest you open your fucking ears,
because I'm about to tell it to you.

470
00:33:28.960 --> 00:33:30.803
Go on, Mr. Valentine.

471
00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:32.485
I'm still listening.

472
00:33:33.280 --> 00:33:37.171
As long as you agree to all my terms.

473
00:34:25.360 --> 00:34:26.885
All right, no one panic. Listen to me.

474
00:34:27.160 --> 00:34:28.207
Stay calm.

475
00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:30.040
Fuck.

476
00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:33.405
Loo snorkels, loo snorkels!

477
00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:34.680
Loo snorkels?

478
00:34:34.840 --> 00:34:35.840
Showerheads!

479
00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:37.722
Showerheads?

480
00:34:37.880 --> 00:34:39.325
She's right. Fucking go!

481
00:34:41.240 --> 00:34:43.766
Hey, hang about,
what's wrong with the fucking door?

482
00:36:07.440 --> 00:36:10.250
Congratulations on completing
your first task.

483
00:36:10.520 --> 00:36:13.171
Charlie, Roxy, well done.

484
00:36:13.320 --> 00:36:15.129
For those of you
who are still confused...

485
00:36:15.280 --> 00:36:17.487
if you can get a breathing tube
around a U-bend of a toilet...

486
00:36:17.640 --> 00:36:19.483
you have an unlimited air supply.

487
00:36:19.640 --> 00:36:22.120
Simple physics, worth remembering.

488
00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:25.608
Eggsy, well done for spotting
that was a two-way mirror.

489
00:36:25.760 --> 00:36:26.761
He's probably seen enough of them.

490
00:36:26.920 --> 00:36:29.810
Yeah, you can all wipe those smirks
off your faces.

491
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.800
Because as far as I'm concerned,
every single one of you has failed.

492
00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:37.209
You all forgot
the most important thing...

493
00:36:38.200 --> 00:36:39.486
teamwork.

494
00:36:53.680 --> 00:36:56.331
So much for classic army technique.

495
00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:00.760
35.

496
00:37:01.440 --> 00:37:02.805
105.

497
00:37:03.440 --> 00:37:05.761
That's it. That's it.

498
00:37:10.360 --> 00:37:11.360
Hello.

499
00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:12.847
Can I help you?

500
00:37:13.040 --> 00:37:16.408
Yes. I have a question
about anthropogenic force.

501
00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:21.009
Really? It's actually quite fascinating.

502
00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:24.530
My colleague died
trying to rescue you...

503
00:37:24.720 --> 00:37:26.404
and I'm sure you saw
how well trained he was...

504
00:37:26.560 --> 00:37:29.200
so I suggest you tell me who kidnapped
you and why they let you go.

505
00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:31.084
I have no idea what you're talking...

506
00:37:31.880 --> 00:37:34.121
I'm not supposed to say it, but it was...

507
00:37:34.520 --> 00:37:36.204
For God's sake, I've barely touched you.

508
00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:37.691
Man up!

509
00:37:58.520 --> 00:38:00.443
Fuck that guy, whoever he is.
I'm gonna...

510
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:03.968
He made me kill Professor Arnold.

511
00:38:04.120 --> 00:38:05.451
I goddamn loved Professor Arnold.

512
00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:06.681
Well, the good news is...

513
00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:08.649
we know the emergency
and surveillance system work.

514
00:38:08.800 --> 00:38:10.768
You know what's not good news?

515
00:38:10.920 --> 00:38:12.649
"My colleague died!"

516
00:38:12.800 --> 00:38:14.211
That's what he said!

517
00:38:14.360 --> 00:38:16.727
This is an organization,
and they're all over us.

518
00:38:16.960 --> 00:38:18.724
- Whoever you spoke to...
- I told you...

519
00:38:18.880 --> 00:38:22.441
I made contact with the KGB, MI6,
Mossad and Beijing.

520
00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:24.200
They all insist he wasn't one of theirs.

521
00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:25.726
Beijing.

522
00:38:26.160 --> 00:38:30.404
So freaky how there's no recognizable name
for the Chinese secret service.

523
00:38:30.840 --> 00:38:33.002
Now, that's what you call
a secret, right?

524
00:38:34.040 --> 00:38:35.769
You know what? Fuck it.

525
00:38:36.240 --> 00:38:37.810
We need to speed things up.

526
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:39.360
Bring the product release forward.

527
00:38:39.480 --> 00:38:41.323
We're only halfway into production...

528
00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:42.925
and speeding it will cost a fortune.

529
00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:44.366
Do I look like I give a fuck?

530
00:38:44.600 --> 00:38:46.443
Just get it done.

531
00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:51.531
As some of you will
have learned last night...

532
00:38:52.960 --> 00:38:56.169
teamwork is paramount here at Kingsman.

533
00:38:56.320 --> 00:39:00.120
We're here to enhance your skills,
test you to the limit.

534
00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:03.727
Which is why you're gonna pick a puppy.

535
00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:05.723
Wherever you go, your dog goes.

536
00:39:05.880 --> 00:39:08.087
You will care for it. You will teach it.

537
00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:11.329
And by the time it's fully trained,
so will you be.

538
00:39:11.480 --> 00:39:14.086
Those of you who are still here,
that is.

539
00:39:14.240 --> 00:39:16.163
Do you understand?

540
00:39:16.360 --> 00:39:18.249
Choose your puppy.

541
00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:22.081
A poodle?

542
00:39:22.240 --> 00:39:23.240
What?

543
00:39:23.320 --> 00:39:24.924
They're gun dogs.

544
00:39:25.080 --> 00:39:26.570
Oldest working breed.

545
00:39:26.760 --> 00:39:28.524
Easy to train.

546
00:39:29.560 --> 00:39:30.846
A pug?

547
00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:33.884
It's a bulldog, innit?

548
00:39:36.320 --> 00:39:37.720
It'll get bigger, though, won't it?

549
00:39:41.600 --> 00:39:43.728
Shit.

550
00:39:45.720 --> 00:39:49.042
His MRI shows no signs of concussion.

551
00:39:49.240 --> 00:39:52.210
No direct brain trauma at all.

552
00:39:52.520 --> 00:39:54.602
How much longer can he be out?

553
00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:55.921
That's the million-dollar question.

554
00:39:56.120 --> 00:39:57.929
We don't know
what he was exposed to in there.

555
00:39:58.120 --> 00:39:59.565
What about Harry's footage?

556
00:39:59.720 --> 00:40:01.404
It didn't stream to his home terminal.

557
00:40:01.560 --> 00:40:04.530
Encrypted and uncrackable.

558
00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:05.960
If and when he comes around...

559
00:40:06.080 --> 00:40:08.686
you might want to have a word with him
about sharing his password.

560
00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:10.530
Is he gonna be all right?

561
00:40:11.720 --> 00:40:13.370
We need to have patience, Eggsy.

562
00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:15.131
But there's hope, okay?

563
00:40:15.720 --> 00:40:17.404
If I were you,
I'd concentrate on your training.

564
00:40:17.600 --> 00:40:19.762
Make it through the tests.
Make him proud.

565
00:40:27.400 --> 00:40:28.890
Come on, come on, come on!

566
00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:31.122
J.B., come on! Come on!

567
00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:36.242
I'm not coming last because of you.

568
00:40:37.080 --> 00:40:39.560
J.B., I'll shoot you!
Goddamn you, I'll fucking shoot you!

569
00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:42.484
Merlin said we're not
allowed to hold you.

570
00:40:44.640 --> 00:40:46.165
Bollocks.

571
00:41:28.680 --> 00:41:29.680
Water!

572
00:41:32.960 --> 00:41:34.450
- Come on, then!
- Eggsy, forget it!

573
00:41:34.600 --> 00:41:36.240
What's wrong, mate?
You can't take a joke?

574
00:41:36.280 --> 00:41:38.442
Seriously, you'll get thrown out,
and it's just not worth it.

575
00:41:38.640 --> 00:41:40.130
Maybe I don't give a fuck
if I get kicked out!

576
00:41:40.280 --> 00:41:41.645
Do it. Come on, you pleb.

577
00:41:41.800 --> 00:41:43.211
Charlie, fuck off!

578
00:41:45.320 --> 00:41:48.290
Yeah, go on, walk away. Dickhead.

579
00:41:49.640 --> 00:41:50.721
Come on, J.B.

580
00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:51.961
Come on, good boy.

581
00:42:05.760 --> 00:42:08.161
You have exactly one hour
to complete the test...

582
00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:09.890
starting now.

583
00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:13.689
<i>New target, 800 meters.</i>

584
00:42:13.880 --> 00:42:15.484
<i>You know, it's unbelievable.
You're still here...</i>

585
00:42:15.640 --> 00:42:19.167
lingering like some
big, steaming shit that just won't flush.

586
00:42:19.320 --> 00:42:20.845
Roger that. Target identified.

587
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:23.002
And how about you shut the fuck up?

588
00:42:23.160 --> 00:42:24.286
Positive discrimination...

589
00:42:24.440 --> 00:42:25.885
that's what it is.

590
00:42:26.040 --> 00:42:29.203
It's like those fucking state school kids
who get into Oxford on C grades...

591
00:42:29.400 --> 00:42:31.040
because their mum
is a one-legged lesbian.

592
00:42:31.160 --> 00:42:32.760
You don't know fuck all about my grades.

593
00:42:32.840 --> 00:42:34.729
Forgive me,
I'm sure you're highly educated.

594
00:42:34.880 --> 00:42:36.370
Fire when ready.

595
00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:40.522
How's that for positive discrimination?

596
00:42:53.200 --> 00:42:55.009
I want to thank you both
for listening...

597
00:42:55.160 --> 00:42:58.243
and I really, really appreciate
you travelling all this way...

598
00:42:58.400 --> 00:42:59.401
Your Royal Highness.

599
00:42:59.760 --> 00:43:01.364
And you, too, Prime Minister.

600
00:43:01.520 --> 00:43:04.569
I think this is quite brilliant.

601
00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:07.566
It's absolutely brilliant.

602
00:43:08.320 --> 00:43:11.164
You are completely crazy.

603
00:43:13.200 --> 00:43:14.770
And as for you, Prime Minister

604
00:43:14.880 --> 00:43:17.087
I'm speechless you'd even consider this.

605
00:43:22.400 --> 00:43:25.370
- Don't touch...
- Sorry, Your Royal Highness.

606
00:43:25.520 --> 00:43:26.567
But you've got a big role to play...

607
00:43:26.720 --> 00:43:29.291
in getting the Scandinavian
region back on track.

608
00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:30.965
You're popular, inspirational...

609
00:43:31.120 --> 00:43:33.566
and you have the power
to galvanize the people.

610
00:43:33.720 --> 00:43:36.564
Now, whether you're on board or not...

611
00:43:36.720 --> 00:43:38.370
I'm going to have to insist...

612
00:43:38.520 --> 00:43:41.410
on getting you somewhere
I can ensure your safety.

613
00:43:41.920 --> 00:43:44.127
How about you, Prime Minister?
You in or out?

614
00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:46.605
Well, I think it's about time...

615
00:43:46.760 --> 00:43:51.448
that a politician did something
that actually made a difference.

616
00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:53.763
Too true.

617
00:43:53.920 --> 00:43:54.762
What?

618
00:43:54.920 --> 00:43:56.251
Take her away.

619
00:43:59.920 --> 00:44:00.920
Drink?

620
00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:03.285
Why not?

621
00:44:05.200 --> 00:44:07.168
Guards! Help!

622
00:44:07.240 --> 00:44:07.968
Don't worry.

623
00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:09.605
No harm will come to the princess.

624
00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:14.250
Well, I'm a republican anyways,
so it really doesn't matter.

625
00:44:15.760 --> 00:44:16.760
Release the princess!

626
00:44:50.480 --> 00:44:51.641
Okay, you're done.

627
00:44:51.800 --> 00:44:53.325
Not so bad, right?

628
00:44:53.840 --> 00:44:55.683
Hardly felt a thing.

629
00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:57.490
Welcome aboard.

630
00:44:57.960 --> 00:44:59.803
Pleasure is all mine.

631
00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:07.121
Ever heard of knocking?

632
00:45:08.320 --> 00:45:09.760
Only when I'm casing a place to rob.

633
00:45:11.160 --> 00:45:12.480
Merlin said you wanted to see me?

634
00:45:13.640 --> 00:45:15.688
I hope J.B.'s training
is going as well as yours is.

635
00:45:15.960 --> 00:45:17.007
Sit.

636
00:45:19.520 --> 00:45:22.410
Congratulations on making it
to the final six candidates.

637
00:45:22.560 --> 00:45:25.040
Your test results were even better
than I could've hoped.

638
00:45:27.680 --> 00:45:28.841
Come in.

639
00:45:33.040 --> 00:45:35.691
Eggsy, I need to have
a private conversation.

640
00:45:35.840 --> 00:45:36.840
You're dismissed.

641
00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:38.684
Nonsense. Let him observe.

642
00:45:38.920 --> 00:45:40.524
Might learn a thing or two.

643
00:45:41.040 --> 00:45:43.042
As you wish. Take a look at this.

644
00:45:43.200 --> 00:45:45.009
<i>For God's sake, I've barely touched you.</i>

645
00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:46.160
<i>Man up!</i>

646
00:45:46.680 --> 00:45:48.364
Fucking hell!

647
00:45:48.520 --> 00:45:50.488
That is rank, Harry.

648
00:45:51.200 --> 00:45:52.565
You blew up his head?

649
00:45:52.720 --> 00:45:54.165
It's a bit much, innit?

650
00:45:54.320 --> 00:45:58.006
Actually, the explosion was caused
by an implant in his neck.

651
00:45:58.200 --> 00:45:59.725
Here, under the scar.

652
00:46:00.040 --> 00:46:02.566
Did my hardware
pick up the signal that triggered it?

653
00:46:02.720 --> 00:46:04.245
Fortunately, yes.

654
00:46:04.560 --> 00:46:06.528
Unfortunately,
the IP address I traced it to...

655
00:46:06.680 --> 00:46:08.887
is registered
to the Valentine Corporation.

656
00:46:09.040 --> 00:46:11.884
That's not much of a lead.
He has millions of employees worldwide.

657
00:46:12.080 --> 00:46:14.242
That Richmond Valentine is a genius.

658
00:46:17.840 --> 00:46:20.047
Did you not see his announcement today?

659
00:46:20.720 --> 00:46:21.926
No.

660
00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:29.521
<i>We each spend on average
$2,000 a year...</i>

661
00:46:29.720 --> 00:46:31.609
<i>on cell phone and internet usage.</i>

662
00:46:31.760 --> 00:46:34.889
<i>It gives me great pleasure
to announce...</i>

663
00:46:35.040 --> 00:46:37.611
<i>those days are over.</i>

664
00:46:37.760 --> 00:46:38.807
<i>As of tomorrow...</i>

665
00:46:38.960 --> 00:46:42.806
<i>every man, woman and child
can claim a free SIM card...</i>

666
00:46:42.960 --> 00:46:47.090
<i>compatible with any cell phone,
any computer...</i>

667
00:46:47.280 --> 00:46:51.444
<i>and utilize my communications network
for free.</i>

668
00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:52.931
<i>Free calls...</i>

669
00:46:53.120 --> 00:46:54.610
<i>free internet...</i>

670
00:46:54.760 --> 00:46:56.285
for everyone.

671
00:46:57.280 --> 00:46:58.611
<i>Forever.</i>

672
00:47:14.440 --> 00:47:17.125
Valentine's assistant
has the same implant scar.

673
00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:20.291
I think Mr. Valentine and I
should have a tête-à-tête.

674
00:47:23.800 --> 00:47:26.280
He's having a gala dinner next week.

675
00:47:26.440 --> 00:47:29.284
I'll get you an invitation.
You need to be careful, though.

676
00:47:29.480 --> 00:47:31.448
Since you've been out,
hundreds of VIPs have gone missing.

677
00:47:31.600 --> 00:47:33.967
No ransom notes,
exactly like Professor Arnold.

678
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:38.041
Then I suggest you make my alias
somebody worth kidnapping.

679
00:47:50.840 --> 00:47:52.001
<i>Fuck, fuck, fuck!</i>

680
00:47:52.160 --> 00:47:53.321
<i>What, don't like heights?</i>

681
00:47:53.480 --> 00:47:54.481
<i>Yeah, it's okay.</i>

682
00:47:54.720 --> 00:47:58.327
<i>I've done it before, which is probably why,
come to think of it.</i>

683
00:47:59.640 --> 00:48:01.529
<i>Hey, it's gonna be all right.</i>

684
00:48:01.680 --> 00:48:03.125
<i>You're top of the class.</i>

685
00:48:05.120 --> 00:48:06.360
<i>Listen up.</i>

686
00:48:06.520 --> 00:48:09.330
<i>Your mission is to land in the target
without the radar detecting you.</i>

687
00:48:09.480 --> 00:48:13.166
If I read you on the radar,
or you miss the target, you go home.

688
00:48:13.520 --> 00:48:14.681
Is that understood?

689
00:48:18.200 --> 00:48:20.806
<i>Drop zone coming up, 20 seconds.</i>

690
00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:23.571
<i>We gotta go.</i>

691
00:48:32.840 --> 00:48:34.729
<i>Eggsy, I really don't think
I can do this.</i>

692
00:48:34.880 --> 00:48:35.881
<i>Of course you can't.</i>

693
00:48:36.040 --> 00:48:37.800
<i>Head to the back
and I'll show you how, yeah?</i>

694
00:48:45.880 --> 00:48:47.882
<i>Eggsy, wait! Hang on!</i>

695
00:48:48.880 --> 00:48:50.405
<i>Roxy, just stop fucking about!</i>

696
00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:53.000
<i>Follow me, yeah?</i>

697
00:49:07.080 --> 00:49:08.923
<i>Come on!</i>

698
00:49:10.200 --> 00:49:12.248
<i>Roxy, it's now or never.</i>

699
00:49:13.520 --> 00:49:14.760
<i>Jump!</i>

700
00:49:33.400 --> 00:49:34.731
<i>Good girl, Rox...</i>

701
00:49:34.880 --> 00:49:36.484
<i>I'm glad you made it!</i>

702
00:49:49.280 --> 00:49:50.964
<i>Yeah!</i>

703
00:49:51.600 --> 00:49:52.601
<i>Come on!</i>

704
00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:57.128
My, my, you're all very cheerful.

705
00:49:57.280 --> 00:49:59.561
Did you really think it was gonna be
that straightforward?

706
00:49:59.640 --> 00:50:02.007
Any idiot can read a heads-up display.

707
00:50:02.160 --> 00:50:05.846
A Kingsman agent needs to be able
to solve problems under pressure.

708
00:50:06.440 --> 00:50:09.922
Like what to do when one of
your group has no parachute.

709
00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:12.970
<i>- What, no parachute?
- Shit!</i>

710
00:50:13.360 --> 00:50:14.486
<i>Who?</i>

711
00:50:14.640 --> 00:50:15.482
<i>Fuck!</i>

712
00:50:15.640 --> 00:50:16.640
<i>Which one?</i>

713
00:50:16.760 --> 00:50:18.205
<i>What do we do?</i>

714
00:50:18.360 --> 00:50:19.771
<i>I told you. Aim for the target.</i>

715
00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:21.206
<i>Come in under the radar.</i>

716
00:50:21.360 --> 00:50:23.328
And I hope not to be scraping
one of you up.

717
00:50:23.680 --> 00:50:26.650
But if I do have to,
and you're inside the target...

718
00:50:27.160 --> 00:50:28.844
please know I'll be very impressed.

719
00:50:29.040 --> 00:50:30.451
<i>- Fuck!
- Oh, shit!</i>

720
00:50:34.320 --> 00:50:36.004
<i>Everybody listen, I've got a plan!</i>

721
00:50:37.720 --> 00:50:40.690
<i>Pair off!
Grab the closest person to them.</i>

722
00:50:43.320 --> 00:50:44.526
<i>Rufus, come on!</i>

723
00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:45.720
<i>Fuck!</i>

724
00:50:46.520 --> 00:50:47.520
<i>Rufus!</i>

725
00:50:47.840 --> 00:50:49.001
<i>Shit! I can't!</i>

726
00:50:52.840 --> 00:50:53.840
<i>Fuck!</i>

727
00:50:54.880 --> 00:50:56.006
<i>Thank God!</i>

728
00:50:56.160 --> 00:50:58.003
<i>Rufus, you wanker!</i>

729
00:50:59.240 --> 00:51:00.651
<i>Shit, we're an odd number now!</i>

730
00:51:01.720 --> 00:51:02.801
<i>Quick, make a circle!</i>

731
00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:04.689
<i>Fuck, he's right! Boys, let's do it.</i>

732
00:51:09.400 --> 00:51:11.482
<i>We pull our cords one by one!</i>

733
00:51:11.640 --> 00:51:12.880
<i>When we know who's fucked...</i>

734
00:51:13.040 --> 00:51:14.520
<i>the person on their right grabs them.</i>

735
00:51:16.160 --> 00:51:17.400
<i>Okay, Eggsy.</i>

736
00:51:17.880 --> 00:51:18.881
<i>Good plan, Eggsy.</i>

737
00:51:19.040 --> 00:51:21.202
You have 30 seconds.
Come on now, hurry.

738
00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:22.361
<i>Me first!</i>

739
00:51:24.880 --> 00:51:25.722
<i>Fuck!</i>

740
00:51:25.880 --> 00:51:27.211
<i>Yes!</i>

741
00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:31.686
<i>Okay, me next.</i>

742
00:51:33.680 --> 00:51:35.205
<i>See you on the ground, boys.</i>

743
00:51:39.040 --> 00:51:40.041
<i>Now me.</i>

744
00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:44.920
<i>Fuck!</i>

745
00:51:49.400 --> 00:51:50.208
<i>Roxy...</i>

746
00:51:50.360 --> 00:51:52.400
<i>No matter what happens now,
I've got you, all right?</i>

747
00:51:55.920 --> 00:51:57.206
<i>Okay, Eggsy.</i>

748
00:51:57.360 --> 00:51:58.521
<i>- Yours first, okay?
- Yep.</i>

749
00:52:11.720 --> 00:52:12.720
Shit!

750
00:52:20.400 --> 00:52:21.640
<i>Shit!</i>

751
00:52:23.760 --> 00:52:24.760
<i>Shit!</i>

752
00:52:26.440 --> 00:52:27.440
<i>Rox!</i>

753
00:52:30.880 --> 00:52:32.006
<i>Fuck.</i>

754
00:52:48.320 --> 00:52:50.527
<i>Hugo, Digby.</i>

755
00:52:50.680 --> 00:52:53.490
You don't land in the K,
you're not in the K.

756
00:52:53.640 --> 00:52:55.961
Rufus, you opened too soon.

757
00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:57.485
You were all over the radar.

758
00:52:57.640 --> 00:52:59.483
All three of you,
pack your bags, go home.

759
00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:03.807
Eggsy, Roxy, congratulations.

760
00:53:04.120 --> 00:53:05.770
You set a new record.

761
00:53:05.920 --> 00:53:07.160
Opening at 300 feet...

762
00:53:07.320 --> 00:53:08.367
that's pretty ballsy.

763
00:53:08.520 --> 00:53:11.046
Well done for completing another task.
Fall out.

764
00:53:12.160 --> 00:53:13.161
Sorry, sir.

765
00:53:13.320 --> 00:53:15.004
But why the fuck did you
choose me as the gimp?

766
00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:16.366
Am I the expendable candidate?

767
00:53:16.520 --> 00:53:19.126
No, no, no.
You don't talk to me like that.

768
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:21.840
You have a complaint, you come here
and you whisper it in my ear.

769
00:53:28.320 --> 00:53:31.051
You need to take
that chip off your shoulder.

770
00:54:02.040 --> 00:54:04.520
Mr. DeVere.
It's a pleasure to meet you.

771
00:54:05.160 --> 00:54:07.891
I'm awfully sorry.
I seem to have my dates muddled up.

772
00:54:08.040 --> 00:54:10.930
No, no, no.
I cancelled the gala because of you.

773
00:54:11.240 --> 00:54:13.049
Anybody willing to donate that much...

774
00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:15.362
deserves their own dinner.
Come in!

775
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:18.001
Thank you.

776
00:54:19.880 --> 00:54:22.406
Got to admit,
I was really intrigued to meet you.

777
00:54:22.560 --> 00:54:24.403
There aren't many billionaires
I don't know.

778
00:54:24.560 --> 00:54:25.561
I don't doubt it.

779
00:54:25.720 --> 00:54:28.724
And, obviously,
I had my people look into your affairs...

780
00:54:28.880 --> 00:54:30.640
and that's some pretty old money
you're from.

781
00:54:30.760 --> 00:54:31.760
How'd your folks make it?

782
00:54:32.240 --> 00:54:35.244
Property, mostly.
Property and the markets.

783
00:54:35.400 --> 00:54:37.448
Nothing questionable,
if that's your concern.

784
00:54:37.600 --> 00:54:40.365
Look, I'm just into finding out
what caliber person you are.

785
00:54:40.520 --> 00:54:41.680
I'm sure you understand that.

786
00:54:41.920 --> 00:54:42.967
I most certainly do.

787
00:54:43.120 --> 00:54:44.610
- Hope you're hungry.
- I'm famished.

788
00:54:44.800 --> 00:54:45.847
Good.

789
00:54:45.920 --> 00:54:46.921
Grab a seat.

790
00:55:08.680 --> 00:55:09.880
I'll have the Big Mac, please.

791
00:55:09.920 --> 00:55:11.126
Great choice.

792
00:55:11.280 --> 00:55:14.682
But nothing beats two cheeseburgers
with secret sauce.

793
00:55:14.840 --> 00:55:16.649
Goes great with this '45 Lafite.

794
00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:17.801
A classic pairing.

795
00:55:18.240 --> 00:55:21.244
And may I suggest Twinkies
and a 1937 Château d'Yquem for pudding?

796
00:55:22.080 --> 00:55:23.445
I like it.

797
00:55:24.040 --> 00:55:27.840
So, you want to donate to my foundation.

798
00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:31.322
You are aware that I wound things
down in that area, right?

799
00:55:31.480 --> 00:55:34.404
Climate change is a threat,
which affects us all, Mr. Valentine.

800
00:55:34.600 --> 00:55:37.729
And you're one of the few powerful men
who seems to share my concerns.

801
00:55:37.880 --> 00:55:40.565
No, I shut things down,
because I wasn't getting anywhere.

802
00:55:40.720 --> 00:55:43.564
Every bit of research
kept pointing to the same thing.

803
00:55:43.720 --> 00:55:45.085
That carbon emissions
are a red herring...

804
00:55:45.240 --> 00:55:48.926
and that we're past the point of no return
no matter what remedial actions we take?

805
00:55:49.320 --> 00:55:50.924
You know your shit.

806
00:55:51.080 --> 00:55:54.687
I sometimes envy the blissful ignorance
of those less well versed in their...

807
00:55:55.240 --> 00:55:56.446
"shit."

808
00:55:57.480 --> 00:55:59.050
As Professor Arnold always said...

809
00:55:59.600 --> 00:56:02.046
"Humankind is the only virus
cursed to live...

810
00:56:02.200 --> 00:56:05.443
"with the horrifying knowledge
of its host's fragile mortality."

811
00:56:06.680 --> 00:56:09.251
You know, not a lot of people
knew about him.

812
00:56:11.960 --> 00:56:14.327
You like spy movies, Mr. DeVere?

813
00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:21.049
Nowadays, they're all a little
serious for my taste.

814
00:56:21.200 --> 00:56:22.200
But the old ones...

815
00:56:22.960 --> 00:56:24.200
Marvelous.

816
00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:26.641
Give me a far-fetched
theatrical plot any day.

817
00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:30.327
The old Bond movies. Oh, man!

818
00:56:30.480 --> 00:56:34.007
When I was a kid, that was my dream job.

819
00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:36.404
Gentleman spy.

820
00:56:36.760 --> 00:56:40.128
I always felt the old Bond films
were only as good as the villain.

821
00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:44.610
As a child, I rather fancied a future
as a colorful megalomaniac.

822
00:56:46.480 --> 00:56:49.802
What a shame we both had to grow up.

823
00:56:54.400 --> 00:56:55.640
<i>Bon appétit.</i>

824
00:56:58.160 --> 00:57:01.130
Just give me a couple of days
to think over your proposal.

825
00:57:01.280 --> 00:57:02.884
I'll have my people
get in touch with yours...

826
00:57:03.040 --> 00:57:04.565
and it's all good.

827
00:57:04.720 --> 00:57:08.247
And thank you for such a happy meal.

828
00:57:13.600 --> 00:57:14.965
Well, want me to follow him?

829
00:57:15.160 --> 00:57:16.286
Nah.

830
00:57:16.560 --> 00:57:19.006
I put a nano tracker gel in the wine.

831
00:57:19.200 --> 00:57:22.204
We'll know his every move
for the next 24 hours.

832
00:57:22.360 --> 00:57:24.931
Finally find out who he works for.

833
00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:28.448
Valentine didn't let me
out of his sight.

834
00:57:28.600 --> 00:57:31.126
All I got was this on the way in.

835
00:57:35.240 --> 00:57:38.323
South Glade Mission Church
is a hate group based in Kentucky.

836
00:57:39.200 --> 00:57:40.804
FBI have been monitoring them for years.

837
00:57:40.960 --> 00:57:42.769
But you think Valentine is a supporter?

838
00:57:42.920 --> 00:57:46.208
No evidence yet of a direct connection,
but I'll keep looking.

839
00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:48.491
By the way...

840
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:53.680
our ever-growing list of missing persons
now includes Scandinavian royalty.

841
00:57:54.080 --> 00:57:56.811
Royal Crown Princess Tilde.

842
00:57:58.880 --> 00:58:01.724
Just let me out, you psycho!

843
00:58:01.880 --> 00:58:04.724
I told you, you're free to go
any time you want.

844
00:58:04.880 --> 00:58:07.167
As long as you agree to my conditions.

845
00:58:07.560 --> 00:58:09.210
I don't agree...

846
00:58:09.360 --> 00:58:12.091
and I am never ever going to agree!

847
00:58:12.240 --> 00:58:13.480
Tough shit.

848
00:58:13.920 --> 00:58:14.921
Bitch.

849
00:58:17.080 --> 00:58:18.844
I want to speak to the British Council!

850
00:58:19.440 --> 00:58:23.889
<i>The list of missing celebrities and dignitaries
has continued to grow in recent weeks...</i>

851
00:58:24.040 --> 00:58:27.931
<i>and world leaders are coming under
increasing pressure to provide answers.</i>

852
00:58:28.080 --> 00:58:31.846
<i>We are doing everything in our power
to find Princess Tilde.</i>

853
00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:35.163
<i>You know,
governments and security forces worldwide...</i>

854
00:58:35.360 --> 00:58:39.046
<i>are working together to find the person
behind these abductions.</i>

855
00:58:39.240 --> 00:58:40.920
<i>In other news,
people all over the world...</i>

856
00:58:41.040 --> 00:58:45.443
<i>continue to wait in line day and night
to get their free SIM cards.</i>

857
00:58:45.600 --> 00:58:48.080
Mrs. P, did you get one?

858
00:58:48.240 --> 00:58:50.811
Yeah, I've been queuing up all day.

859
00:58:51.000 --> 00:58:55.244
<i>This unprecedented giveaway
by the philanthropist Richmond Valentine...</i>

860
00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:58.244
<i>has already seen
over a billion cards distributed.</i>

861
00:58:58.400 --> 00:58:59.640
At ease.

862
00:59:01.800 --> 00:59:04.201
So you thought we were done
for the day, huh?

863
00:59:05.000 --> 00:59:06.206
Well, we're not.

864
00:59:07.840 --> 00:59:09.842
- A party?
- Tonight, in London.

865
00:59:11.600 --> 00:59:13.921
- Who's this?
- Your target.

866
00:59:14.080 --> 00:59:16.048
Your mission
is to use your NLP training...

867
00:59:16.200 --> 00:59:18.640
to win over the individual
on the photograph in your envelope.

868
00:59:18.760 --> 00:59:20.285
And when I say "win over"...

869
00:59:20.600 --> 00:59:22.250
I do mean in the biblical sense.

870
00:59:22.400 --> 00:59:23.561
Easy.

871
00:59:24.480 --> 00:59:26.528
Posh girls love a bit of rough.

872
00:59:26.680 --> 00:59:28.330
We'll see about that, yeah?

873
00:59:28.600 --> 00:59:30.409
We certainly will.

874
00:59:35.600 --> 00:59:36.600
Hi!

875
00:59:36.760 --> 00:59:40.048
Sorry, I just had to come over
and say, amazing eyes.

876
00:59:40.400 --> 00:59:41.640
Are you wearing color contacts?

877
00:59:41.800 --> 00:59:44.007
- No!
- You so are.

878
00:59:44.160 --> 00:59:46.561
Oh, my God, negging! That's hilarious.

879
00:59:46.720 --> 00:59:48.609
I haven't heard anyone try that
since the noughties.

880
00:59:48.760 --> 00:59:49.886
Excuse me?

881
00:59:50.040 --> 00:59:51.040
"Negging."

882
00:59:51.080 --> 00:59:55.051
Saying something negative to a pretty girl
in order to undermine her social value.

883
00:59:55.200 --> 00:59:57.282
It's supposed to make you
want to win his approval.

884
00:59:57.840 --> 01:00:00.889
Absurdly basic
neuro-linguistic programming technique.

885
01:00:01.040 --> 01:00:03.202
Is it just me, or does this champagne
taste a little bit funny?

886
01:00:03.360 --> 01:00:05.249
- It's an acquired taste, mate.
- I think it's just cheap.

887
01:00:05.400 --> 01:00:07.243
Get one of these instead.
They're delicious.

888
01:00:07.400 --> 01:00:10.131
If you're into seduction techniques,
this guy is textbook.

889
01:00:10.280 --> 01:00:13.045
See what he just did?
It's called an opinion opener.

890
01:00:13.200 --> 01:00:14.690
He got you talking
with a neutral question...

891
01:00:14.880 --> 01:00:16.640
got all of us involved
in the conversation...

892
01:00:16.720 --> 01:00:18.404
so that you craved individual attention.

893
01:00:19.120 --> 01:00:20.451
No, I'm just saying
the champagne tastes rank.

894
01:00:20.600 --> 01:00:22.364
Lady Sophie Montague-Herring.

895
01:00:22.520 --> 01:00:23.851
Phone call for you at reception.

896
01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:25.840
- Be right back.
- We'll see you in a bit, yeah?

897
01:00:25.880 --> 01:00:27.245
See you in a bit.

898
01:00:27.400 --> 01:00:29.243
Budge up, Rox. I'm feeling a bit rough.

899
01:00:29.400 --> 01:00:30.925
- Are you all right?
- No.

900
01:00:31.080 --> 01:00:32.127
Sorry to eavesdrop...

901
01:00:32.280 --> 01:00:35.841
but there's a much easier way
to guarantee getting someone home.

902
01:00:36.040 --> 01:00:37.610
Rohypnol.

903
01:00:39.760 --> 01:00:41.524
Or even something stronger.

904
01:00:59.080 --> 01:01:00.764
Who the fuck are you?

905
01:01:01.320 --> 01:01:02.765
Where am I?

906
01:01:05.160 --> 01:01:06.321
This knife...

907
01:01:06.480 --> 01:01:08.562
can save your life.

908
01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:13.801
Fuck!

909
01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:17.010
My employer's got two questions
for you, Eggsy.

910
01:01:17.160 --> 01:01:19.049
What the fuck is Kingsman?

911
01:01:19.200 --> 01:01:20.850
And who's Harry Hart?

912
01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:22.843
I don't know who the fuck that is!

913
01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:23.808
Shit!

914
01:01:23.960 --> 01:01:27.760
Eggsy, I just killed two of your friends
who gave me the same bullshit answer!

915
01:01:28.400 --> 01:01:29.400
Fuck!

916
01:01:29.760 --> 01:01:32.331
Just cut the fucking ropes, please!

917
01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:33.527
Hey, Eggsy!

918
01:01:33.680 --> 01:01:35.045
Is Kingsman worth dying for?

919
01:01:37.240 --> 01:01:38.605
Fuck you!

920
01:01:52.920 --> 01:01:54.206
Congratulations.

921
01:01:54.360 --> 01:01:55.600
Bloody well done.

922
01:01:57.880 --> 01:01:59.484
How did the others do?

923
01:01:59.640 --> 01:02:01.449
Roxy passed with flying colors.

924
01:02:01.960 --> 01:02:04.247
Charlie's up next. Want to watch?

925
01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:07.085
Yeah, all right.

926
01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:11.648
Is Kingsman really worth dying for?

927
01:02:11.800 --> 01:02:13.165
No, it fucking isn't!

928
01:02:13.320 --> 01:02:15.163
Shit, I'll tell you what you want.
Please!

929
01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:16.606
Chester King is Arthur.

930
01:02:16.760 --> 01:02:19.001
Arthur's head of a spy agency.
It's called Kingsman.

931
01:02:19.160 --> 01:02:20.840
- Get me out of here!
- Thank you, Charlie.

932
01:02:20.880 --> 01:02:22.211
Much appreciated.

933
01:02:22.360 --> 01:02:24.761
Come on!
That wasn't the fucking deal!

934
01:02:25.160 --> 01:02:27.447
Fuck!

935
01:02:34.440 --> 01:02:36.761
I had such high hopes for you.

936
01:02:36.960 --> 01:02:38.883
You're a bloody disgrace.

937
01:02:39.040 --> 01:02:40.041
Arthur, I'm sorry.

938
01:02:40.880 --> 01:02:42.211
At least untie me.

939
01:02:42.560 --> 01:02:43.891
Untie yourself.

940
01:02:45.560 --> 01:02:47.722
Arthur, please.

941
01:02:49.040 --> 01:02:51.611
<i>I'm the fucking son of the... Shit!</i>

942
01:02:51.760 --> 01:02:54.286
<i>Anyone? Hello?</i>

943
01:02:54.440 --> 01:02:57.011
Galahad, Percival, congratulations.

944
01:02:57.280 --> 01:03:00.090
Your candidates have reached
the final stage of the testing process.

945
01:03:00.240 --> 01:03:03.801
As tradition allows,
you now have 24 hours to spend with them.

946
01:03:04.400 --> 01:03:07.563
Eggsy, you should know your
father reached this point.

947
01:03:08.320 --> 01:03:09.321
From now on...

948
01:03:09.800 --> 01:03:11.280
there are no safety nets, understood?

949
01:03:15.120 --> 01:03:16.120
Good. Dismissed.

950
01:03:19.960 --> 01:03:22.088
Charlie, time to go home.

951
01:03:22.240 --> 01:03:23.605
<i>Fuck you.</i>

952
01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:26.287
Fucking dad's gonna hear about this!

953
01:03:28.440 --> 01:03:29.441
"To pee or not to pee?"

954
01:03:31.680 --> 01:03:32.522
That was the headline...

955
01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:35.285
the day after I defused
a dirty bomb in Paris.

956
01:03:35.920 --> 01:03:37.604
"Germany, 1, England, 5."

957
01:03:37.760 --> 01:03:38.841
Missed that game.

958
01:03:39.040 --> 01:03:42.010
I was breaking up an undercover
spy ring at the Pentagon.

959
01:03:47.480 --> 01:03:48.811
My first mission.

960
01:03:48.960 --> 01:03:50.760
Foiled the assassination
of Margaret Thatcher.

961
01:03:51.960 --> 01:03:53.640
Not everybody would
thank you for that one.

962
01:03:53.720 --> 01:03:56.451
The point is, Eggsy,
nobody thanked me for any of them.

963
01:03:57.120 --> 01:04:00.681
Front page news on all these occasions
was celebrity nonsense.

964
01:04:00.960 --> 01:04:04.521
Because it's the nature of Kingsman
that our achievements remain secret.

965
01:04:04.960 --> 01:04:08.328
A gentleman's name should appear
in the newspaper only three times.

966
01:04:08.480 --> 01:04:10.801
When he's born, when he marries,
and when he dies.

967
01:04:10.960 --> 01:04:14.169
And we are, first and foremost,
gentlemen.

968
01:04:14.480 --> 01:04:15.811
That's me fucked then.

969
01:04:16.800 --> 01:04:18.689
It's like Charlie said. I'm just a pleb.

970
01:04:18.840 --> 01:04:19.841
Nonsense.

971
01:04:20.040 --> 01:04:22.960
Being a gentleman has nothing to do
with the circumstances of one's birth.

972
01:04:23.480 --> 01:04:25.323
Being a gentleman
is something one learns.

973
01:04:26.080 --> 01:04:27.923
Yeah, but how?

974
01:04:28.840 --> 01:04:30.080
All right, first lesson.

975
01:04:30.240 --> 01:04:32.040
You should've asked me
before you took a seat.

976
01:04:33.520 --> 01:04:34.681
Second lesson...

977
01:04:35.680 --> 01:04:37.011
how to make a proper martini.

978
01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:40.082
Yes, Harry.

979
01:04:42.680 --> 01:04:45.729
Goddamn it! This fucking hurts!

980
01:04:46.200 --> 01:04:48.726
You're the one who asked
for a biometric security system.

981
01:04:48.880 --> 01:04:50.006
What's wrong with a simple switch?

982
01:04:50.160 --> 01:04:51.161
A simple switch?

983
01:04:51.360 --> 01:04:55.001
This is an extremely dangerous machine.

984
01:04:55.200 --> 01:04:59.728
It should only be operated by someone
as responsible and sane as me.

985
01:04:59.920 --> 01:05:02.207
Bad shit could happen
if this falls into the wrong hands.

986
01:05:05.400 --> 01:05:07.084
We done here? Shit!

987
01:05:07.240 --> 01:05:09.891
No. Now this one.

988
01:05:10.040 --> 01:05:11.120
For the test at the church.

989
01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:13.083
This one just has a short range.

990
01:05:13.240 --> 01:05:14.810
A simple switch will do.

991
01:05:20.760 --> 01:05:23.650
So are you gonna teach me how to
talk proper, like in <i>My Fair Lady?</i>

992
01:05:23.800 --> 01:05:25.245
Don't be absurd.

993
01:05:25.560 --> 01:05:28.086
Being a gentleman has nothing
to do with one's accent.

994
01:05:28.240 --> 01:05:30.561
It's about being at ease
in one's own skin.

995
01:05:30.720 --> 01:05:32.290
As Hemingway said,
"There is nothing noble...

996
01:05:32.440 --> 01:05:34.807
"in being superior to your fellow man.

997
01:05:35.240 --> 01:05:38.722
"True nobility is being superior
to your former self."

998
01:05:42.440 --> 01:05:45.762
Now, the first thing every
gentleman needs is a good suit.

999
01:05:45.960 --> 01:05:49.248
By which I mean, a bespoke suit.
Never off-the-peg.

1000
01:05:49.400 --> 01:05:51.801
And Kingsman suits
are always bulletproof.

1001
01:05:51.960 --> 01:05:54.770
So let's get you measured,
and then, whether you get the job or not...

1002
01:05:54.920 --> 01:05:59.289
you'll have a lasting and useful memento
of your time at Kingsman.

1003
01:05:59.440 --> 01:06:03.081
I'm so sorry, sir, but a gentleman
is completing his fitting.

1004
01:06:03.240 --> 01:06:05.447
Fitting Room Two is available.

1005
01:06:05.600 --> 01:06:09.605
One does not use Fitting Room Two
when one is popping one's cherry.

1006
01:06:10.680 --> 01:06:13.490
Perhaps I'll show you Fitting Room Three
while we wait.

1007
01:06:23.840 --> 01:06:25.126
So we going up or down?

1008
01:06:25.280 --> 01:06:26.441
Neither.

1009
01:06:27.680 --> 01:06:28.681
Is this it?

1010
01:06:28.880 --> 01:06:31.963
Of course not.
Pull the hook on your left.

1011
01:06:39.200 --> 01:06:40.200
Oh, yes.

1012
01:06:40.440 --> 01:06:42.647
Very, very nice.

1013
01:06:45.680 --> 01:06:48.160
You're going to need a pair of shoes
to go with your suit.

1014
01:06:48.320 --> 01:06:52.484
An oxford is any formal shoe
with open lacing.

1015
01:06:52.640 --> 01:06:55.849
This additional decorative piece
is called broguing.

1016
01:06:56.000 --> 01:06:57.206
