<i>I see a young man with potential...</i>

1268
01:25:46.600 --> 01:25:49.285
<i>who wants to do something
good with his life.</i>

1269
01:26:05.960 --> 01:26:08.281
Arthur, Harry's dead.

1270
01:26:08.960 --> 01:26:11.361
Galahad is dead.

1271
01:26:11.560 --> 01:26:13.961
Hence, we have just drunk
a toast to him.

1272
01:26:14.640 --> 01:26:17.166
Well, then you know
what that psycho's doing.

1273
01:26:17.320 --> 01:26:19.971
How many people around the world
have got those SIM cards?

1274
01:26:20.120 --> 01:26:22.521
Valentine can send his signal
to any of them, all of them.

1275
01:26:22.680 --> 01:26:24.728
If they all go homicidal
at the same time then...

1276
01:26:24.880 --> 01:26:27.201
Indeed, and thanks
to Galahad's recordings...

1277
01:26:27.360 --> 01:26:29.966
we have Valentine's confession.

1278
01:26:30.160 --> 01:26:33.528
The intelligence has been passed on
to the relevant authorities.

1279
01:26:33.680 --> 01:26:35.045
Our work is complete...

1280
01:26:35.200 --> 01:26:39.649
and a most distinguished legacy
for our fallen friend, it is, too.

1281
01:26:40.480 --> 01:26:41.641
And that's it?

1282
01:26:42.840 --> 01:26:44.001
Come sit down, boy.

1283
01:26:47.360 --> 01:26:52.366
This is an 1815 Napoleonic brandy.

1284
01:26:53.400 --> 01:26:56.688
And we only drink it
when we lose a Kingsman.

1285
01:26:57.320 --> 01:27:00.369
Galahad was very fond of you.

1286
01:27:02.520 --> 01:27:04.921
And on this occasion...

1287
01:27:05.080 --> 01:27:08.448
I think it's acceptable for us
to bend the rules a little.

1288
01:27:10.840 --> 01:27:12.001
Are these all Kingsmen?

1289
01:27:12.200 --> 01:27:14.521
Yes, they're founder members.

1290
01:27:15.880 --> 01:27:17.962
I want you to join me in a toast.

1291
01:27:20.200 --> 01:27:22.202
To Galahad.

1292
01:27:23.200 --> 01:27:24.690
To Galahad.

1293
01:27:29.240 --> 01:27:31.891
Harry says you don't like
to break rules, Arthur.

1294
01:27:32.360 --> 01:27:33.441
Why now?

1295
01:27:33.640 --> 01:27:34.880
You're very good, Eggsy.

1296
01:27:35.040 --> 01:27:38.647
Perhaps I will make you my proposal
for Galahad's position.

1297
01:27:39.560 --> 01:27:42.245
Provided, of course,
that we can see eye to eye...

1298
01:27:42.440 --> 01:27:44.568
on certain political matters.

1299
01:27:47.400 --> 01:27:48.925
Can you guess...

1300
01:27:50.040 --> 01:27:51.644
what this is?

1301
01:27:51.800 --> 01:27:53.484
I don't have to. Harry showed me.

1302
01:27:53.640 --> 01:27:55.165
You click it. I die.

1303
01:27:55.320 --> 01:27:57.129
I thought that brandy tasted a bit shit.

1304
01:27:59.080 --> 01:28:00.080
Bravo.

1305
01:28:00.400 --> 01:28:03.563
Valentine won you over, somehow.

1306
01:28:03.720 --> 01:28:06.564
Once he explained, I understood.

1307
01:28:06.760 --> 01:28:08.000
<i>When you get a virus...</i>

1308
01:28:08.280 --> 01:28:09.486
you get a fever.

1309
01:28:09.640 --> 01:28:13.690
That's the human body raising
its core temperature to kill the virus.

1310
01:28:13.840 --> 01:28:16.081
Planet Earth works the same way.

1311
01:28:16.240 --> 01:28:18.163
Global warming is the fever.

1312
01:28:18.320 --> 01:28:21.130
Mankind is the virus.

1313
01:28:21.280 --> 01:28:23.681
We're making our planet sick.

1314
01:28:23.840 --> 01:28:26.446
A cull is our only hope.

1315
01:28:26.600 --> 01:28:28.841
If we don't reduce
our population ourselves...

1316
01:28:29.000 --> 01:28:31.606
there is only one of two ways
this can go.

1317
01:28:31.760 --> 01:28:36.004
The host kills the virus,
or the virus kills the host.

1318
01:28:36.320 --> 01:28:37.320
Either way...

1319
01:28:38.240 --> 01:28:39.810
The result is the same.

1320
01:28:40.000 --> 01:28:41.604
The virus dies.

1321
01:28:42.680 --> 01:28:46.127
So Valentine's gonna take care
of the population problem himself.

1322
01:28:46.280 --> 01:28:48.806
Well, if we don't do something,
nature will.

1323
01:28:48.960 --> 01:28:53.284
Sometimes a culling is the only way
to ensure that this species survives...

1324
01:28:54.000 --> 01:28:56.128
and history will see Valentine...

1325
01:28:56.280 --> 01:28:58.567
as the man who saved
humanity from extinction.

1326
01:28:59.120 --> 01:29:02.488
And he gets to pick and choose
who gets culled, does he?

1327
01:29:02.640 --> 01:29:03.846
All his rich mates, they get to live...

1328
01:29:04.000 --> 01:29:06.526
and anyone he thinks is worth saving,
he's keeping them safe...

1329
01:29:06.680 --> 01:29:08.648
whether they agree with him or not.

1330
01:29:08.800 --> 01:29:10.962
And you, Eggsy.

1331
01:29:11.520 --> 01:29:13.488
In Harry's honor...

1332
01:29:13.640 --> 01:29:18.328
I am inviting you
to be part of a new world.

1333
01:29:20.400 --> 01:29:22.687
It's time to make your decision.

1334
01:29:29.560 --> 01:29:31.528
I'd rather be with Harry.

1335
01:29:32.160 --> 01:29:33.160
Thanks.

1336
01:29:33.840 --> 01:29:35.205
So be it.

1337
01:29:51.520 --> 01:29:54.763
The problem with us common types...

1338
01:29:54.920 --> 01:29:56.524
is that we're light-fingered.

1339
01:29:57.720 --> 01:29:59.449
Kingsman's taught me a lot...

1340
01:29:59.600 --> 01:30:00.840
but sleight of hand...

1341
01:30:01.520 --> 01:30:03.284
Yes, they're founder members.

1342
01:30:05.920 --> 01:30:07.206
I had that down already.

1343
01:30:09.520 --> 01:30:13.127
You dirty little fucking...

1344
01:30:13.280 --> 01:30:14.725
prick.

1345
01:30:49.000 --> 01:30:50.729
It's okay, Lancelot. Put it down.

1346
01:30:51.920 --> 01:30:53.445
It's verified.

1347
01:30:55.840 --> 01:30:58.411
Arthur's phone is receiving update
texts about getting to safety.

1348
01:30:58.560 --> 01:31:00.324
- We don't have a lot of time.
- What are you going to do?

1349
01:31:00.480 --> 01:31:02.642
The question is,
what are we going to do?

1350
01:31:02.800 --> 01:31:05.531
God knows who's in Valentine's pocket
and who's not.

1351
01:31:06.160 --> 01:31:07.685
We have no choice.

1352
01:31:08.760 --> 01:31:10.842
We are gonna have to deal
with this ourselves.

1353
01:31:14.280 --> 01:31:15.611
Follow me.

1354
01:31:34.480 --> 01:31:35.811
What the fuck is this?

1355
01:31:35.960 --> 01:31:37.803
I have no idea.

1356
01:31:38.800 --> 01:31:39.961
What you're playing with...

1357
01:31:40.120 --> 01:31:42.851
is a prototype personal
transatmospheric vehicle.

1358
01:31:43.000 --> 01:31:45.287
It was developed as part of
Reagan's Star Wars project.

1359
01:31:45.440 --> 01:31:48.364
It's pretty basic,
but it should still work.

1360
01:31:48.640 --> 01:31:51.007
We're gonna take out
one of Valentine's satellites.

1361
01:31:51.400 --> 01:31:53.846
We're gonna break the chain,
stop the signal.

1362
01:31:54.000 --> 01:31:55.920
It'll take him a couple of hours
to reroute it...

1363
01:31:56.360 --> 01:32:00.729
which buys us enough time for you
to get me into Valentine's mainframe...

1364
01:32:00.880 --> 01:32:02.689
so I can shut it down.

1365
01:32:02.840 --> 01:32:05.161
Lancelot, you're going to be using it.

1366
01:32:05.320 --> 01:32:06.685
Get into your halo suit.

1367
01:32:19.320 --> 01:32:21.440
<i>Swedish Prime Minister,
requesting permission to land.</i>

1368
01:32:27.080 --> 01:32:28.844
<i>Permission granted.</i>

1369
01:32:32.440 --> 01:32:34.920
- Please.
- Thank you.

1370
01:32:35.080 --> 01:32:37.162
- How many more are we expecting?
- Not many.

1371
01:32:37.360 --> 01:32:38.691
Most have their own bunkers.

1372
01:32:38.840 --> 01:32:42.208
I figure we're just getting
the really nervous ones.

1373
01:32:42.440 --> 01:32:44.442
Welcome, Prime Minister.

1374
01:32:45.720 --> 01:32:48.690
It seems the implant
can emit some kind of counter signal...

1375
01:32:48.840 --> 01:32:52.526
to ensure the wearer remains unaffected
by the waves from the SIM cards.

1376
01:32:52.680 --> 01:32:54.728
The waves that turn everyone
into a psycho killer.

1377
01:32:54.920 --> 01:32:57.446
Quite. But what he
probably didn't tell anyone...

1378
01:32:57.600 --> 01:33:01.889
is it can also super heat
their soft tissue at his command.

1379
01:33:02.040 --> 01:33:06.204
Valentine selected his chosen few
to get the countdown warning...

1380
01:33:06.360 --> 01:33:09.204
but he had to be sure they didn't blab
to the wrong people beforehand.

1381
01:33:09.360 --> 01:33:11.089
How does this help us right now?

1382
01:33:12.040 --> 01:33:13.041
It doesn't.

1383
01:33:13.440 --> 01:33:14.805
Roxy, here we go!

1384
01:33:27.720 --> 01:33:31.327
The higher you go,
the more the balloons expand.

1385
01:33:31.480 --> 01:33:33.323
When you reach
the edge of the atmosphere...

1386
01:33:33.480 --> 01:33:35.608
they'll explode.

1387
01:33:35.760 --> 01:33:37.762
You'll need to deploy your missile
just before that, okay?

1388
01:33:37.960 --> 01:33:39.291
Edge of the atmosphere.

1389
01:33:39.440 --> 01:33:42.762
And once you've deployed,
you'll need to release for descent, fast.

1390
01:33:43.760 --> 01:33:45.000
Good luck.

1391
01:33:47.320 --> 01:33:49.322
- You can do this, okay?
- Yeah.

1392
01:33:49.480 --> 01:33:52.290
Eggsy, come on. Time is not our friend.

1393
01:34:14.760 --> 01:34:16.762
You're getting in
on Arthur's invitation.

1394
01:34:16.960 --> 01:34:18.166
You're gonna need to blend in.

1395
01:34:18.320 --> 01:34:19.446
I'm supposed to be Arthur?

1396
01:34:19.600 --> 01:34:22.604
His invitation is in his phone.
You give them this.

1397
01:34:22.800 --> 01:34:25.280
- Give his real name, Chester King.
- What about you?

1398
01:34:25.440 --> 01:34:26.885
I'm your pilot.
I'm gonna stay here.

1399
01:34:27.960 --> 01:34:29.041
Is that gonna fit me?

1400
01:34:29.200 --> 01:34:31.726
A bespoke suit always fits.

1401
01:34:31.880 --> 01:34:33.689
Just be grateful
Harry had it made for you.

1402
01:34:34.640 --> 01:34:35.641
Get dressed.

1403
01:34:37.080 --> 01:34:38.360
What the fuck's wrong with them?

1404
01:34:38.480 --> 01:34:41.211
I don't know. Could have something to do
with the mass genocide.

1405
01:34:41.400 --> 01:34:43.323
Give me the mic.

1406
01:34:45.120 --> 01:34:46.690
<i>Hey-oh!</i>

1407
01:34:46.840 --> 01:34:49.764
<i>Everybody, listen up! Hello, hello!</i>

1408
01:34:49.920 --> 01:34:52.161
<i>What the fuck is wrong with you people?</i>

1409
01:34:52.320 --> 01:34:55.164
<i>I just wanna remind you that today...</i>

1410
01:34:55.320 --> 01:34:57.926
<i>is a day of celebration.</i>

1411
01:34:58.720 --> 01:35:02.247
<i>We must put aside
all thoughts of death...</i>

1412
01:35:02.400 --> 01:35:04.289
<i>and focus on birth.</i>

1413
01:35:05.360 --> 01:35:07.806
<i>The birth of a new age.</i>

1414
01:35:09.000 --> 01:35:13.961
<i>We mustn't mourn those
who give their lives today.</i>

1415
01:35:14.120 --> 01:35:16.088
<i>We should honor their sacrifice...</i>

1416
01:35:16.240 --> 01:35:18.242
Has she got my number to call me back?
I got a new phone.

1417
01:35:18.440 --> 01:35:21.603
<i>...and their roles in saving
the human race.</i>

1418
01:35:24.000 --> 01:35:27.686
<i>We must put aside doubt and guilt.</i>

1419
01:35:29.080 --> 01:35:32.641
<i>You are the chosen people.</i>

1420
01:35:34.280 --> 01:35:37.727
<i>When folks tell their kids
the story of Noah's Ark...</i>

1421
01:35:37.880 --> 01:35:38.880
<i>is Noah the bad guy?</i>

1422
01:35:39.040 --> 01:35:39.689
No!

1423
01:35:39.840 --> 01:35:41.888
<i>Is God the bad guy?</i>

1424
01:35:42.040 --> 01:35:42.689
No!

1425
01:35:42.880 --> 01:35:45.281
<i>How about the animals
marching two by two?</i>

1426
01:35:45.440 --> 01:35:46.248
No!

1427
01:35:46.400 --> 01:35:47.400
<i>Of course not!</i>

1428
01:35:48.320 --> 01:35:49.685
<i>Yeah, that's it!</i>

1429
01:35:49.840 --> 01:35:53.640
<i>Let's turn those frowns upside down.</i>

1430
01:35:53.800 --> 01:35:55.643
<i>Eat, drink...</i>

1431
01:35:55.800 --> 01:35:57.484
<i>and Party!</i>

1432
01:36:00.520 --> 01:36:03.046
<i>And I will see you all in the new age.</i>

1433
01:36:28.280 --> 01:36:30.408
<i>Rox, it's me.</i>

1434
01:36:30.920 --> 01:36:32.251
<i>How's the view?</i>

1435
01:36:35.080 --> 01:36:37.162
- Hideous
<i>- Mine's pretty sweet.</i>

1436
01:36:37.320 --> 01:36:40.244
- They made you one of these suits yet?
<i>- No, not yet.</i>

1437
01:36:40.440 --> 01:36:42.761
<i>You've got something to
look forward to then.</i>

1438
01:36:42.920 --> 01:36:45.526
<i>We're coming up on Valentine's base.
Gotta go.</i>

1439
01:36:46.960 --> 01:36:48.291
<i>Good luck.</i>

1440
01:36:55.920 --> 01:36:56.921
Looking good, Eggsy.

1441
01:36:59.600 --> 01:37:02.331
Feeling good, Merlin.

1442
01:37:07.600 --> 01:37:09.204
<i>This is November-2-4-7-Charlie-Kilo.</i> ..

1443
01:37:09.360 --> 01:37:11.806
<i>Requesting permission to land.</i>

1444
01:37:14.800 --> 01:37:17.326
<i>Permission is granted.</i>

1445
01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:22.809
Fuck me.

1446
01:37:50.000 --> 01:37:52.446
Eggsy, we're on.

1447
01:38:07.160 --> 01:38:08.161
Chester King.

1448
01:38:09.160 --> 01:38:11.128
Mr. King, welcome.

1449
01:38:11.520 --> 01:38:15.320
I'm sure you've adhered to Valentine's
strict no-weapons policy...

1450
01:38:15.480 --> 01:38:16.811
- but if you don't object...
- Of course.

1451
01:38:16.960 --> 01:38:18.200
Thank you.

1452
01:38:18.680 --> 01:38:20.808
Do you have any luggage?

1453
01:38:21.800 --> 01:38:25.247
Congratulations, Mycroft,
you just graduated from my pilot to my valet.

1454
01:38:25.840 --> 01:38:28.320
- You cheeky...
Understood?

1455
01:38:28.480 --> 01:38:29.720
Good.

1456
01:38:31.040 --> 01:38:32.644
Thank you.

1457
01:38:57.920 --> 01:39:02.562
<i>Eggsy, find a laptop, get me online.
The clock is ticking.</i>

1458
01:39:03.720 --> 01:39:06.451
<i>And remember, try to blend in.</i>

1459
01:39:06.600 --> 01:39:08.568
Would sir care for a drink?

1460
01:39:09.200 --> 01:39:10.406
Martini.

1461
01:39:10.560 --> 01:39:12.722
Gin, not vodka, obviously.

1462
01:39:12.920 --> 01:39:16.606
Stirred for 10 seconds while glancing
at an unopened bottle of vermouth.

1463
01:39:17.240 --> 01:39:18.446
Thank you.

1464
01:39:21.240 --> 01:39:23.049
Merlin, are you clocking this?

1465
01:39:23.240 --> 01:39:25.288
Yes, I am. Stay focused.

1466
01:39:25.920 --> 01:39:28.082
Lancelot, you're doing great.
Not much further to go.

1467
01:39:28.800 --> 01:39:29.926
<i>Yes, Merlin.</i>

1468
01:39:31.440 --> 01:39:33.727
<i>Eggsy, get me online now.</i>

1469
01:39:34.640 --> 01:39:35.641
Yep, I'm on it.

1470
01:39:36.800 --> 01:39:38.928
Lancelot, you're approaching
your altitude limit.

1471
01:39:39.280 --> 01:39:41.044
<i>Those balloons won't last much longer.</i>

1472
01:39:41.920 --> 01:39:43.888
<i>Prepare to engage missile.</i>

1473
01:39:59.280 --> 01:40:00.486
Society's dead.

1474
01:40:00.960 --> 01:40:02.803
Long live society.

1475
01:40:03.800 --> 01:40:05.131
Amen to that.

1476
01:40:06.600 --> 01:40:08.648
- I'm Morten Lindström.
- Chester King.

1477
01:40:08.960 --> 01:40:10.291
How'd you get online? I couldn't.

1478
01:40:10.680 --> 01:40:13.650
It's a closed network, you see.
Pre-authorized connections only.

1479
01:40:17.840 --> 01:40:19.126
<i>I've got a fix on the satellite.</i>

1480
01:40:19.320 --> 01:40:20.480
<i>Do you have the correct time?</i>

1481
01:40:20.600 --> 01:40:21.806
I think I'm still in my last time zone.

1482
01:40:21.960 --> 01:40:23.371
Yeah, yeah. Let's see now.

1483
01:40:37.440 --> 01:40:38.441
Eggsy, I'm in.

1484
01:40:38.600 --> 01:40:39.726
Get your arse back to the plane, now.

1485
01:40:39.880 --> 01:40:41.450
<i>- On my way.</i>
- Lancelot, good luck!

1486
01:40:41.600 --> 01:40:43.807
Firing in 3... 2...

1487
01:40:51.160 --> 01:40:52.161
Nice and slow.

1488
01:40:52.320 --> 01:40:53.526
Fuck are you doing here?

1489
01:40:53.680 --> 01:40:56.001
Well, my family were invited, obviously.

1490
01:40:56.160 --> 01:40:57.810
Now, get the fuck up! Slowly.

1491
01:40:59.000 --> 01:41:00.889
Shit. Lancelot, hurry up and fire!

1492
01:41:01.040 --> 01:41:02.644
<i>That other balloon is gonna blow!</i>

1493
01:41:02.800 --> 01:41:05.849
<i>Yes, Merlin. I've nearly got it.
Give me a second!</i>

1494
01:41:07.720 --> 01:41:10.644
Valentine! I've caught a fucking spy!

1495
01:41:11.320 --> 01:41:12.367
V-Glass, zoom.

1496
01:41:12.520 --> 01:41:14.568
Oh, fuck! It's that young valet.

1497
01:41:18.680 --> 01:41:20.091
Son of a bitch.

1498
01:41:20.640 --> 01:41:21.766
<i>Got it!</i>

1499
01:41:31.880 --> 01:41:33.166
Oh, shit. Sound the alarm!

1500
01:41:35.720 --> 01:41:36.800
I'm not taking any chances.

1501
01:41:36.920 --> 01:41:38.560
Okay, you send out
the two-minute warning.

1502
01:41:38.600 --> 01:41:41.046
I'm starting the override.
All right, let's do this.

1503
01:41:42.400 --> 01:41:44.004
<i>Countdown initiated.</i>

1504
01:41:53.720 --> 01:41:55.404
- You see him?
- Right here.

1505
01:42:04.200 --> 01:42:05.440
Eggsy, take a left.

1506
01:42:06.240 --> 01:42:07.241
Two guards, up ahead.

1507
01:42:19.600 --> 01:42:20.886
Lancelot! Release now!

1508
01:42:31.920 --> 01:42:33.729
<i>Eggsy, straight ahead, then right.</i>

1509
01:42:34.120 --> 01:42:35.121
<i>There's two more.</i>

1510
01:42:38.800 --> 01:42:40.928
<i>All right, everybody on your feet!</i>

1511
01:42:41.080 --> 01:42:42.286
<i>Countdown to V-day!</i>

1512
01:42:42.440 --> 01:42:43.965
<i>Welcome in the new age!</i>

1513
01:42:52.320 --> 01:42:53.401
<i>Flat spin.</i>

1514
01:43:08.600 --> 01:43:11.444
<i>Eggsy, next left,
down the narrow tunnel!</i>

1515
01:43:20.200 --> 01:43:21.201
Here we go!

1516
01:43:21.360 --> 01:43:22.360
10...

1517
01:43:23.000 --> 01:43:24.331
<i>9...</i>

1518
01:43:24.840 --> 01:43:25.840
<i>8...</i>

1519
01:43:26.480 --> 01:43:27.480
<i>7...</i>

1520
01:43:28.400 --> 01:43:29.400
<i>6...</i>

1521
01:43:30.080 --> 01:43:31.161
5...

1522
01:43:31.760 --> 01:43:32.760
<i>4...</i>

1523
01:43:34.000 --> 01:43:34.762
<i>3...</i>

1524
01:43:34.920 --> 01:43:35.920
2...

1525
01:43:36.680 --> 01:43:37.680
1!

1526
01:43:43.600 --> 01:43:45.443
Nice! Well done, both of you.

1527
01:43:46.160 --> 01:43:47.161
It's not working!

1528
01:43:47.360 --> 01:43:49.408
It's supposed to be working!
What the fuck?

1529
01:43:56.200 --> 01:43:56.849
<i>Yes!</i>

1530
01:43:57.040 --> 01:43:58.371
Well done, Rox. Good girl.

1531
01:44:01.720 --> 01:44:04.246
We've lost one of our satellites.

1532
01:44:13.800 --> 01:44:17.566
Oh, no, no.
There's no way I can hack past that.

1533
01:44:23.120 --> 01:44:24.121
What's going on?

1534
01:44:25.320 --> 01:44:26.401
Is there a problem?

1535
01:44:27.560 --> 01:44:28.920
Come on. There's no need for guns.

1536
01:44:29.040 --> 01:44:30.565
I'm just a pilot.

1537
01:44:33.560 --> 01:44:34.607
Fuck. Merlin!

1538
01:44:37.400 --> 01:44:39.004
Get in here!

1539
01:44:43.240 --> 01:44:44.401
Come on!

1540
01:44:47.960 --> 01:44:49.291
Let's get the fuck out of here!

1541
01:44:49.440 --> 01:44:50.441
We can't.

1542
01:44:50.600 --> 01:44:52.090
I can't get into Valentine's machine.

1543
01:44:52.240 --> 01:44:53.844
He's got biometric security.

1544
01:44:55.320 --> 01:44:58.642
You're gonna have to get in there and make
sure his hand never touches that desk.

1545
01:44:58.800 --> 01:45:00.325
Are you taking the fucking piss?

1546
01:45:00.520 --> 01:45:01.760
I'm afraid not.

1547
01:45:04.920 --> 01:45:05.921
Let's have that then.

1548
01:45:07.600 --> 01:45:08.931
This is mine.

1549
01:45:09.440 --> 01:45:11.363
I'll show you yours.

1550
01:45:28.680 --> 01:45:29.680
Good choice.

1551
01:45:32.320 --> 01:45:33.920
How long to re-link the satellite chain?

1552
01:45:34.040 --> 01:45:35.280
It'll take an hour, maybe two.

1553
01:45:35.440 --> 01:45:37.568
Bullshit! Just bring these two
closer together.

1554
01:45:37.720 --> 01:45:39.051
But that's not yours.

1555
01:45:44.720 --> 01:45:46.484
V-Glass, call E-man.

1556
01:45:47.280 --> 01:45:48.645
E, it's V.

1557
01:45:48.800 --> 01:45:50.802
Listen, man,
I got a little hiccup on this end.

1558
01:45:50.960 --> 01:45:51.961
I need to piggyback.

1559
01:45:52.120 --> 01:45:56.170
One of my satellites just went down,
but it's right next to one of yours.

1560
01:45:56.680 --> 01:45:58.170
You read my mind.

1561
01:45:58.800 --> 01:46:00.404
How long before you make that happen?

1562
01:46:03.480 --> 01:46:04.527
Go.

1563
01:46:08.680 --> 01:46:10.648
All right, we should be
coming back online.

1564
01:46:13.560 --> 01:46:14.560
10 percent.

1565
01:46:17.680 --> 01:46:18.408
Shit!

1566
01:46:18.600 --> 01:46:20.364
Eggsy, Valentine's using
someone else's satellite.

1567
01:46:20.560 --> 01:46:22.528
<i>He's going to reconnect the chain.</i>

1568
01:46:22.680 --> 01:46:24.200
<i>It's going to take him no time at all.</i>

1569
01:46:25.080 --> 01:46:26.161
It's at 20 percent.

1570
01:46:44.120 --> 01:46:47.363
Eggsy, it seems Valentine's got a present for you.
Get a move on!

1571
01:47:20.880 --> 01:47:22.291
Is that Kingsman kid dead yet?

1572
01:47:22.480 --> 01:47:24.130
Not yet, but he will be soon.

1573
01:47:24.280 --> 01:47:26.009
Good.

1574
01:47:38.920 --> 01:47:39.921
Merlin, I'm fucked.

1575
01:47:53.120 --> 01:47:54.121
As am I.

1576
01:47:54.320 --> 01:47:56.641
They're coming at me from both sides.
I'm out of options.

1577
01:47:57.080 --> 01:47:59.924
Rox, I need a favor.

1578
01:48:00.080 --> 01:48:01.161
Call my mum.

1579
01:48:01.320 --> 01:48:02.920
Tell her to lock herself away from Dean.

1580
01:48:03.640 --> 01:48:04.640
<i>And the baby...</i>

1581
01:48:06.160 --> 01:48:07.161
and tell her I love her.

1582
01:48:16.120 --> 01:48:17.360
For fuck's sake.

1583
01:48:21.720 --> 01:48:24.883
Merlin, remember those implants
you said were of no use to us?

1584
01:48:26.680 --> 01:48:27.960
Any chance you can turn them on?

1585
01:48:31.560 --> 01:48:32.322
All right.

1586
01:48:32.520 --> 01:48:34.966
My turn to play, Valentine.

1587
01:48:43.480 --> 01:48:44.641
Oh, no!

1588
01:48:44.800 --> 01:48:47.246
What the fuck is he doing?
I can't stop this.

1589
01:49:00.640 --> 01:49:01.721
Yes, please.

1590
01:49:05.360 --> 01:49:06.566
No!

1591
01:50:03.320 --> 01:50:05.402
<i>Oh, my God!</i>

1592
01:50:05.560 --> 01:50:07.562
That is fucking spectacular!

1593
01:50:07.720 --> 01:50:10.485
Merlin, you're a fucking genius!

1594
01:50:10.640 --> 01:50:13.803
What the fuck is happening out there?

1595
01:50:18.120 --> 01:50:19.406
Aren't you that princess
who went missing?

1596
01:50:19.560 --> 01:50:20.607
Can you get me out?

1597
01:50:21.240 --> 01:50:23.163
If I do, will you give me a kiss?

1598
01:50:23.320 --> 01:50:24.840
I've always wanted to kiss a princess.

1599
01:50:24.920 --> 01:50:27.480
If you get me out right now,
I'll give you more than just a kiss.

1600
01:50:29.160 --> 01:50:30.400
<i>You motherfucker.</i>

1601
01:50:30.600 --> 01:50:32.409
<i>Did you really think
I was stupid enough...</i>

1602
01:50:32.600 --> 01:50:34.762
<i>to implant one of those
things in my own head?</i>

1603
01:50:35.200 --> 01:50:36.770
<i>What are you, fucking crazy?</i>

1604
01:50:37.720 --> 01:50:40.007
All those innocent people killed
and for what?

1605
01:50:40.880 --> 01:50:43.724
You didn't stop shit!

1606
01:50:45.080 --> 01:50:47.082
Fine, I've locked the door.
What do you want me to do now?

1607
01:50:47.280 --> 01:50:50.124
As I said, put your daughter
in the bathroom and throw away the key.

1608
01:50:50.880 --> 01:50:53.281
It's still happening!

1609
01:50:53.440 --> 01:50:54.601
You're fucking insane!

1610
01:50:54.760 --> 01:50:55.886
<i>Just do it.</i>

1611
01:51:23.200 --> 01:51:24.565
Eggsy, the signal's started!

1612
01:51:24.720 --> 01:51:27.883
Get Valentine's hand off
that bloody desk now!

1613
01:51:28.040 --> 01:51:29.040
Sorry, love.

1614
01:51:29.400 --> 01:51:30.481
Got to save the world.

1615
01:51:31.760 --> 01:51:33.683
I'll be right back.

1616
01:51:35.120 --> 01:51:36.120
Good luck!

1617
01:51:42.880 --> 01:51:43.880
London.

1618
01:52:12.320 --> 01:52:13.320
Rio.

1619
01:52:29.320 --> 01:52:30.320
Get down!

1620
01:52:32.320 --> 01:52:33.320
You did it!

1621
01:52:42.760 --> 01:52:44.683
The glass is not gonna hold long.

1622
01:52:46.360 --> 01:52:47.964
You stay here.

1623
01:52:50.200 --> 01:52:51.361
Merlin, quickly, how do I get up there?

1624
01:52:51.680 --> 01:52:53.603
- Keep shooting, I'll find a route.
- Understood.

1625
01:53:10.160 --> 01:53:11.241
Holy fuck!

1626
01:53:29.760 --> 01:53:31.046
We're back up.

1627
01:53:31.920 --> 01:53:33.251
We're back up!

1628
01:53:40.240 --> 01:53:41.969
This is great!

1629
01:53:50.080 --> 01:53:50.922
<i>Eggsy!</i>

1630
01:53:51.080 --> 01:53:52.605
Fucking get on with it!

1631
01:53:52.800 --> 01:53:54.006
Kick his ass, Gazy!

1632
01:54:00.640 --> 01:54:03.450
Seoul, Caracas, Mumbai!

1633
01:54:11.800 --> 01:54:14.280
Kill that motherfucker!
He killed all our friends!

1634
01:54:31.640 --> 01:54:33.642
Eggsy, the world is going to shit!

1635
01:54:43.040 --> 01:54:45.122
- Is he dead yet?
- Not yet!

1636
01:54:45.280 --> 01:54:47.408
Stop playing with your food!

1637
01:54:47.560 --> 01:54:48.561
Kill him!

1638
01:56:06.680 --> 01:56:08.045
Gazelle!

1639
01:56:09.880 --> 01:56:11.041
Gazelle!

1640
01:56:20.680 --> 01:56:22.409
Come on! Come on!

1641
01:56:25.400 --> 01:56:26.400
<i>Kill him!</i>

1642
01:56:43.720 --> 01:56:44.720
Hey!

1643
01:57:09.440 --> 01:57:10.965
<i>Well done, son!</i>

1644
01:57:12.280 --> 01:57:13.280
Yes!

1645
01:57:13.400 --> 01:57:14.561
Yes, Eggsy!

1646
01:57:14.720 --> 01:57:16.290
Well done, Eggsy!

1647
01:57:16.800 --> 01:57:17.961
And you, Lancelot.

1648
01:57:20.720 --> 01:57:23.291
I'm so sorry.
Mummy would never hurt you.

1649
01:57:23.920 --> 01:57:26.969
Mummy would never hurt you.
I'm so sorry.

1650
01:57:29.440 --> 01:57:30.487
Are you okay?

1651
01:57:34.240 --> 01:57:36.129
Harry would be proud of you, Eggsy.

1652
01:57:37.480 --> 01:57:38.561
He was right.

1653
01:57:54.000 --> 01:57:55.286
What's up, man?

1654
01:57:55.640 --> 01:57:59.008
Is this the part where you say
some really bad pun?

1655
01:58:00.480 --> 01:58:02.482
Well, it's like you said to Harry.

1656
01:58:05.680 --> 01:58:08.001
This ain't that kind of movie, bruv.

1657
01:58:09.480 --> 01:58:10.925
Perfect.

1658
01:58:31.800 --> 01:58:33.006
Eggsy, where are you going?

1659
01:58:33.160 --> 01:58:35.400
There's no need for champagne.
We got loads in the plane.

1660
01:58:42.520 --> 01:58:43.601
Did you save the world?

1661
01:58:44.200 --> 01:58:45.690
Yes, I did.

1662
01:58:47.000 --> 01:58:49.810
So, you gonna come in?

1663
01:58:50.560 --> 01:58:52.050
Yes, I am.

1664
01:58:57.520 --> 01:58:59.409
Merlin, the cell's locked.
How do I get in?

1665
01:59:01.680 --> 01:59:03.205
26-25.

1666
01:59:07.560 --> 01:59:10.166
Merlin, you're the guvnor.

1667
01:59:12.360 --> 01:59:14.727
<i>You owe me, Eggsy.</i>

1668
01:59:20.360 --> 01:59:21.407
Eggsy?

1669
01:59:27.400 --> 01:59:29.084
Oh, my word.

1670
02:00:16.280 --> 02:00:19.124
Michelle, turn that shit off.
It's doing my nut in.

1671
02:00:20.120 --> 02:00:21.645
I rather like that song.

1672
02:00:22.160 --> 02:00:23.764
Leave it on, eh, Mum?

1673
02:00:27.520 --> 02:00:29.443
Mugsy's back.

1674
02:00:29.560 --> 02:00:31.960
You've finally come
to have that word with me, have you, son?

1675
02:00:32.360 --> 02:00:33.720
Or are you gonna run away again...

1676
02:00:33.800 --> 02:00:35.404
and pretend you're going to court,
dressed like that?

1677
02:00:35.840 --> 02:00:37.251
Oh, you mean this?

1678
02:00:38.760 --> 02:00:40.091
No.

1679
02:00:40.680 --> 02:00:44.002
I know this bloke who's just taken over
a tailor shop on Savile Row.

1680
02:00:45.080 --> 02:00:46.650
He's given me a job, Mum.

1681
02:00:47.360 --> 02:00:48.646
It comes with a lot of perks.

1682
02:00:50.040 --> 02:00:51.371
Including a house.

1683
02:00:52.520 --> 02:00:54.363
Come and live with me there, Mum.

1684
02:00:54.960 --> 02:00:56.041
Come on.

1685
02:00:56.200 --> 02:00:57.200
Sit down, you.

1686
02:00:58.320 --> 02:01:00.560
Only place she'll be visiting
is you in fucking hospital.

1687
02:01:00.680 --> 02:01:02.489
- Do you hear?
- Just leave him alone, Dean!

1688
02:01:02.640 --> 02:01:04.881
Eggsy, just go. Please, just go, babe.

1689
02:01:06.360 --> 02:01:07.646
All right.

1690
02:01:07.800 --> 02:01:09.370
That's it, do as Mummy says.

1691
02:01:09.520 --> 02:01:12.364
Why don't you ask that tailor friend of yours,
and knock up a nice chicken costume.

1692
02:01:12.520 --> 02:01:13.885
It'll suit you, you mug.

1693
02:01:16.160 --> 02:01:18.925
As a good friend once said...

1694
02:01:20.240 --> 02:01:21.366
"Manners...

1695
02:01:23.280 --> 02:01:24.280
"maketh...

1696
02:01:26.840 --> 02:01:27.841
"man."

1697
02:01:28.680 --> 02:01:31.047
- Dean?
- Shut the fuck up.

1698
02:01:31.200 --> 02:01:33.646
Eggsy, I'm gonna shove your manners
up your fucking...

1699
02:01:39.600 --> 02:01:40.600
So...

1700
02:01:40.840 --> 02:01:44.845
are we gonna stand around here all day,
or are we gonna fight?
